# GENERATED by tools/gen_quests.py from design/quests/*.toml. Do not edit; edit the TOML and regenerate.
{
	chapter.168ED6F9995F242C.chapter_subtitle: [
		"The Mortal Nether: forests of fungus, bastions and everything that wants your gold."
		"The Mortal Nether is a place for this life only, and it does not mind that. Bridge every gap, keep a stack of cobblestone, never mine the block you are standing on, and carry something fireproof. The Realm below the Realm is not an enemy; it is only indifferent, and that is worse."
	]
	chapter.168ED6F9995F242C.title: "Beneath the Burning Sky"
	chapter.19428CBFCA3DE31A.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Preparing for the Mortal Dragon, and for what is left after it."
		"Nobody comes back from the Mortal End by being brave alone. Come with gold apples, a water bucket for the endermen, a stack of blocks to build with and armour you trust. Then go in, and leave your doubts at the portal. After it, the island still has secrets for those who survive."
	]
	chapter.19428CBFCA3DE31A.title: "The Dragon's Eve"
	chapter.1CCA857B7EBABCCE.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Bells, trades and the people who live on the road."
		"A village is the nearest thing a mortal has to a country. Learn who lives in it, give its people work and trade with them fairly, and you will find a door that opens when you knock and a roof when it rains."
	]
	chapter.1CCA857B7EBABCCE.title: "Folk of the Realm"
	chapter.2643E12F6E936A65.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Ink, thread, stone and the slow science of potions."
		"The Realm remembers its makers: the scribe, the weaver, the mason, the alchemist. None of them kill anything with their art, and all of them outlive the people who do. Learn a craft and it will be useful in two lives."
	]
	chapter.2643E12F6E936A65.title: "Hand and Cauldron"
	chapter.299887ED3F25AE8B.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Coal, copper, gold and the dark under the dark."
		"What the surface will not give you, the ground will. Go down in steps, light every turn, listen for water and for the click of a skeleton's bow, and never dig straight down. The dark is patient; you do not have to be."
	]
	chapter.299887ED3F25AE8B.title: "Down the Shaft"
	chapter.300D34CBDD2EC27E.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Two hundred thousand orcs are marching on the lake."
		"In the story the Orc Lord Geld, driven by hunger, led a horde out of the south towards the Great Jura Forest. The lizardmen of Lake Siss met it first and asked the new monster town for help. This is the chapter where Tempest stops being a camp and becomes a power."
	]
	chapter.300D34CBDD2EC27E.title: "The Orc Lord"
	chapter.3201C62CEF644AC7.chapter_subtitle: [
		"The Orc War is decided in the marsh."
		"The Orc Lord's army is two hundred thousand mouths and one hunger. Chapter 4 held the marsh; this chapter ends the war. Geld is a king who ate his own, and the forest has two answers for him: stand beside the lizardmen and break him, or kneel to the hunger and take his crown. Whatever road you walk, one of you ends the war and the other ends the Horde."
	]
	chapter.3201C62CEF644AC7.title: "Two Hundred Thousand"
	chapter.36D8E5C05627FA49.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Gazel Dwargo weighs everyone who stands before his throne."
		"You have knelt before the King. Now he wants to know what kind of strength it was. The Hero King has ruled the Armed Nation for three hundred years and has judged every petitioner himself, a sham trial against a smith included. Whatever road you walk, the throne room is where it is measured."
	]
	chapter.36D8E5C05627FA49.title: "The King's Test"
	chapter.378BD420FE635504.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Chores of the forest, repeated every day."
		"Tempest never runs out of work. These jobs reset a day after you claim them; the town pays in bronze coins and the odd potion."
	]
	chapter.378BD420FE635504.title: "Daily Deeds: Jura"
	chapter.3CFEA682A10FDD1C.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Dwargon: a kingdom of smiths behind a white gate."
		"A thousand blocks north of Tempest, at the foot of the Great Canaat Mountains, lies the dwarf kingdom of Dwargon: a neutral trade hub inside a cavern, ruled for three hundred years by the Hero King Gazel Dwargo. It is where Kaijin was judged, and where every smith in the world wants to work."
	]
	chapter.3CFEA682A10FDD1C.title: "The Armed Nation"
	chapter.3DD6FBE383605A48.chapter_subtitle: [
		"You only live once here. What you do decides who you become."
		"Every player lives twice. This is the first life: a plain human in the Mortal Realm. When you die, the Voice of the World judges what you did. Your karma decides which races and skills are offered to your soul in the Tensura world."
	]
	chapter.3DD6FBE383605A48.title: "A Mortal Life"
	chapter.45616B685860E3E6.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Fields, flocks, a smokehouse and a line in the water."
		"Hunger kills more first lives than any skeleton does. Learn to feed yourself from a patch of dirt and a few animals and you will outlast a dozen mortals who rely on luck. This is the slow road to a long life."
	]
	chapter.45616B685860E3E6.title: "Seed and Stock"
	chapter.49DCD771BA645C79.chapter_subtitle: [
		"A camp of goblins, a few dwarves and six new kijin. Help them build a town."
		"It is the days just after the ogres were named. Tempest is still a building site: tents beside the first timber houses, Kaijin's forge smoking on the west road, Shuna's looms in the east, a palisade begun only on one side. Everything you carry in can become part of the town."
	]
	chapter.49DCD771BA645C79.title: "Tempest Rises"
	chapter.60737BD25048CC9D.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Small jobs that come back every day."
		"Every day there is wood to cut, mobs to clear and ground to cover. These quests reset a day after you claim them, for as long as you live, in either life. The rewards are small: food, a few torches and some experience."
	]
	chapter.60737BD25048CC9D.title: "Daily Deeds"
	chapter.6760C91AB2E49228.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Day one, with nothing but your hands."
		"Nobody arrives in the Mortal Realm with a sword. The first hours are small things done in the right order: a log, a table, a fire, a chest, something to hold the dark off. Do them well and the rest of the book is open to you."
	]
	chapter.6760C91AB2E49228.title: "Bare Hands"
	chapter.6789349801D8665A.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Tempest stands. Now say where you stand."
		"The town has walls on one side, a forge, a council and a name that is starting to travel. Everything that grows in the forest has to decide whom it welcomes and what it owes. The goblins call the answer an Oath. The road south of the gate splits in two, one lamp-lit towards Tempest's friends, one dark towards the people nobody else will take in."
	]
	chapter.6789349801D8665A.title: "Crossroads"
	chapter.6989E856E32A68B2.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Biomes, ruins and what the old maps left out."
		"The Mortal Realm is a large world made small by habit. Walk it. There are temples in the sand, huts in the swamp, ships in the sea and old trails under the grass, and each is a day's story told by someone who is not coming back."
	]
	chapter.6989E856E32A68B2.title: "The Long Road"
	chapter.6FBCBA46854DE7E5.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Something old is rising out of Lake Siss."
		"The Orc War left the forest with a federation and a name that carries. Names carry to Clayman's ears too. A whirlpool calamity sealed far from Jura has been waiting for someone to wake it, and somebody with strings in their fingers has decided that someone will be a beast prince who does not know what he is carrying. Whatever road you walk, Charybdis is coming."
	]
	chapter.6FBCBA46854DE7E5.title: "The Whirlpool"
	chapter.71CE6A68642EC8F2.chapter_subtitle: [
		"A roof, a fire, a place of your own."
		"A traveller sleeps wherever the night finds them. A householder sleeps in the same bed every night and wakes in the same room, and that is a kind of long life too. Build somewhere worth coming back to."
	]
	chapter.71CE6A68642EC8F2.title: "Hearth and Home"
	chapter.738ADA3283D061B5.chapter_subtitle: [
		"What you did for other people, and what it all adds up to."
		"A first life is short. The Voice of the World will weigh the dragons you killed, the ground you walked and the things you made, and it will weigh something else too: who was warmer for having met you. This chapter does not ask for any of it. It only leaves a door open."
	]
	chapter.738ADA3283D061B5.title: "A Life That Counts"
	chapter.7BD0671B53FE48F5.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Your second life begins in the Forest of Jura."
		"Your soul has crossed. The Forest of Jura, the monster town of Tempest, the dwarves of Dwargon to the north and Lake Siss to the east: this is the world of Tensura, and you are part of it now."
	]
	chapter.7BD0671B53FE48F5.title: "Reborn"
	file.0000000000000001.title: "OCS Tensura: Two Lives"
	quest.000953FD111E508C.quest_desc: [
		"Slay a hoglin, a piglin and a zombified piglin. Hoglins charge, piglins trade or kill, zombified piglins forgive nothing."
		""
		"&7&o“They do not hate you. It is simply that nothing in the Nether has anything to spare.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor: all three are new kinds of foe (+4 each)."
	]
	quest.000953FD111E508C.title: "Pork of the Nether"
	quest.00ECAE3FA494F924.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a spyglass from two copper ingots and an amethyst shard. Use it to read distant villages, ships and ruins before you walk into them."
		""
		"&7&o“A scout's first lesson: if you can see them with the glass, they cannot yet see you.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly: but a map of what lies ahead means a longer life."
	]
	quest.00ECAE3FA494F924.title: "The Far-Seer"
	quest.014697902F2935D2.quest_desc: [
		"Apply an armour trim at a smithing table: the templates are found in old structures, and the trim shows to everyone who looks at your armour."
		""
		"&7&o“A trimmed breastplate is the only vanity the Realm approves of.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Craft: each use of a smithing table is +2; Faith for the advancement (+2)."
	]
	quest.014697902F2935D2.title: "Make Your Mark"
	quest.01E277329C034ED2.quest_desc: [
		"Survive one full day and night (20 minutes of play). Dig in, wall up, light it up. The dark is where most first lives end."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Longevity: every day survived counts. A soul needs at least 2 days to be judged a Survivor, 7 for a Hero, 30 for a Legend."
	]
	quest.01E277329C034ED2.title: "The First Night"
	quest.02B959E613FF1864.quest_desc: [
		"Slay one of each of the common night stalkers."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor: kinds of foe count far more than numbers: each kind slain once adds 4 Valor karma; mob farms add almost nothing."
	]
	quest.02B959E613FF1864.title: "Know Your Enemy"
	quest.035B523513482452.quest_desc: [
		"Smelt six gold ingots. Gold is soft and useless in a tool, but the Nether and its piglins will want it."
		""
		"&7&o“Gold is the only metal the Realm values more for being useless.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.035B523513482452.title: "A Glint of Gold"
	quest.039E840CEA579BD3.quest_desc: [
		"Carry a hundred and twenty-eight cobblestone. A column of stone beneath your feet is the only way up the towers, and the only way out of a bad fall."
		""
		"&7&o“There is no height the Realm has that a mortal with enough stone cannot reach and, with enough sense, come down from.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.039E840CEA579BD3.title: "A Stack to Build With"
	quest.03A66B17ACC87C45.quest_desc: [
		"Giant ants dig under the fences and eat the crops. Kill six."
	]
	quest.03A66B17ACC87C45.quest_subtitle: "Hunt"
	quest.03A66B17ACC87C45.title: "Ants in the Fields"
	quest.03D7C7B0E21E79DD.quest_desc: [
		"Charybdis is a calamity-class monster, a whirlpool with a body, and in Tensura's own fight it brings water and a swarm with it. Gazel needed 10,000 EP; the sea wants twice that. Reach 20,000 EP and carry a plan, whether it is steel, fire or a party."
	]
	quest.03D7C7B0E21E79DD.quest_subtitle: "20,000 EP"
	quest.03D7C7B0E21E79DD.title: "A Match for the Sea"
	quest.041B0CE4E1347744.quest_desc: [
		"Smelt thirty-two iron ingots. Buckets, rails, shields, armour and anvils all take their share."
		""
		"&7&o“A smith never counts his iron; he counts what is missing.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Craft grows with the work behind it, not the ingots themselves."
	]
	quest.041B0CE4E1347744.title: "An Iron Hoard"
	quest.0421C6ABC740C8F8.quest_desc: [
		"Bread keeps people alive longer than swords do. Hand in 16 wheat."
	]
	quest.0421C6ABC740C8F8.quest_subtitle: "Gather"
	quest.0421C6ABC740C8F8.title: "A Day's Harvest"
	quest.04D78E4AFF3D25A3.quest_desc: [
		"Rimuru's side reached the marsh in time to save Gabiru's troops and the old chieftain, and broke most of the horde before the king himself came forward (anime season 1, episode 13). Stand on the same ground and cut down fifteen orcs; the rest of the army will not stay to see the rest of them."
	]
	quest.04D78E4AFF3D25A3.quest_subtitle: "Break the army"
	quest.04D78E4AFF3D25A3.title: "The Great Clash"
	quest.04FB0C80CDC310C0.quest_desc: [
		"Act I closes whichever road you took. Goblins and wolves, a dragon's cave behind you and a dwarf kingdom ahead: the forest has noticed you, and so has everyone who watches the forest. The next chapter is the road to the Dwarf King."
	]
	quest.04FB0C80CDC310C0.quest_subtitle: "Act I"
	quest.04FB0C80CDC310C0.title: "The Forest Awakens"
	quest.057458900C12E9B2.quest_desc: [
		"Direwolves hunt the forest. In the story they became Tempest Wolves after their pack lost to a slime. Prove you could have stood that night."
	]
	quest.057458900C12E9B2.title: "The Direwolf Pack"
	quest.05F41C817DFF715C.quest_desc: [
		"Reincarnation complete. Your new body, race and skill were shaped by the life you lived before. Check yourself: /ttl life shows what your first life earned."
	]
	quest.05F41C817DFF715C.quest_subtitle: "目を開けて"
	quest.05F41C817DFF715C.title: "Open Your Eyes"
	quest.06A90B80AEA7CEB7.quest_desc: [
		"Find an end city on the outer islands. Towers of purpur, bridges, ships and shulkers; the loot is the best in the Realm."
		""
		"&7&o“Nobody lives there. Someone obviously did.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor for the journey, and every new kind of foe slain (+4 each)."
	]
	quest.06A90B80AEA7CEB7.title: "A City Without Streets"
	quest.07264084AF144E8F.quest_desc: [
		"Burn logs in the furnace until you hold eight lumps of charcoal. Coal may be far away; charcoal is only a forest."
		""
		"&7&o“The charcoal burners of the old forests lived alone and smelled of smoke, and no smith in the Realm could have worked without them.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly: it keeps you in torches, and torches keep you alive."
	]
	quest.07264084AF144E8F.title: "Charcoal Burner"
	quest.074E3BFDC57CA159.quest_desc: [
		"Craft diamond armour."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Faith for the advancement; the diamonds you mined already counted as Craft."
	]
	quest.074E3BFDC57CA159.title: "Cover Me with Diamonds"
	quest.07FC914EC6BBF568.quest_desc: [
		"You walked the Nether's roads, traded with its piglins, rode a lava sea and came back with its reagents. Few mortals do. Tick it off when you are ready for the End; The Ledger (chapter 0j) counts it as a way of life."
		""
		"&7&o“The voices in the valley do not say goodbye. They say, softly, until next time.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor: +20 once for walking the Mortal Nether, and every new kind of foe; this milestone only says you did."
	]
	quest.07FC914EC6BBF568.quest_subtitle: "The Nether milestone"
	quest.07FC914EC6BBF568.title: "Hellwalker"
	quest.0852E11640B8614C.quest_desc: [
		"Mine thirty-two blocks of cobblestone. A furnace, a wall and a stone pick all start from this pile."
		""
		"&7&o“Mortals have been stacking stones against the dark since before the first village had a name.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.0852E11640B8614C.title: "A Pile of Stones"
	quest.09312D44BD363D3C.quest_desc: [
		"You took the Horde's crown, and the crown turned out to be a mouth. Put it down (anime season 1, episode 14: the Disaster dies and the orcs are freed from Starved). A horde that has lost two kings in one day will do whatever the next strong hand tells it."
	]
	quest.09312D44BD363D3C.quest_subtitle: "Defeat the Orc Disaster"
	quest.09312D44BD363D3C.title: "The Champion Falls"
	quest.095E9274F41F9EF9.quest_desc: [
		"Gather 15 bookshelves to enchant at the highest level."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Faith: the more you enchant, the more Faith; 15 shelves make every enchantment count."
	]
	quest.095E9274F41F9EF9.title: "A Proper Library"
	quest.0A91A668AA132C1A.quest_desc: [
		"Use an anvil 5 times: repair, combine, name."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Craft: every use of an anvil adds Craft karma. Craft souls lean towards Dwarves and craft skills."
	]
	quest.0A91A668AA132C1A.title: "Hammer and Anvil"
	quest.0A93A9B14DA30692.quest_desc: [
		"Hand in thirty-two torches for the watchmen who walk the village by night. Dark corners are where trouble starts."
		""
		"&7&o“There is a watchman for every village in the Realm and a torch for every watchman, and the second is the harder to keep.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored: the same rule as the bread, with the same reason to do it."
	]
	quest.0A93A9B14DA30692.title: "Torches for the Night Watch"
	quest.0B48B9D221810B49.quest_desc: [
		"Mine twenty-four coal. It burns hotter than wood and lights a longer road than charcoal."
		""
		"&7&o“The old miners called the first seam a promise, and the second one a bill.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.0B48B9D221810B49.title: "Black Gold"
	quest.0B8768A5E7AC606A.quest_desc: [
		"Gather three wither skeleton skulls, summon the Wither far from anyone's home and slay it."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor +100 and a great foe: it counts towards the Legend tier."
	]
	quest.0B8768A5E7AC606A.title: "The Wither"
	quest.0BA57A81D13A7783.quest_desc: [
		"Break tall grass until you hold sixteen wheat seeds and craft a stone hoe. Seeds are the cheapest wealth in the Realm."
		""
		"&7&o“Every harvest begins as a gamble made by someone who intends to be alive in the autumn.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly: a fed soul lives longer, and days alive are Longevity."
	]
	quest.0BA57A81D13A7783.title: "A Handful of Seed"
	quest.0BF0F708AB55929D.quest_desc: [
		"At night the direwolves come out of the forest. Before the slime came, they were the goblins' fear. Stand at the unfinished palisade by the south gate and drive off six of them."
	]
	quest.0BF0F708AB55929D.title: "The Night of the Direwolves"
	quest.0C06954251677EB4.quest_desc: [
		"Gather thirty-two redstone dust and sixteen lapis lazuli from the deep. One drives clocks and doors, the other feeds enchanting tables."
		""
		"&7&o“A miner who comes back with red under his nails has been somewhere the sun does not shine.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Faith: lapis feeds every enchantment, and each one adds Faith."
	]
	quest.0C06954251677EB4.title: "Red and Blue"
	quest.0C49FE11F89AC5E5.quest_desc: [
		"Stand in a dripstone cave and a lush cave. Hanging stone and glowing berries; neither is quite what the surface teaches you to expect."
		""
		"&7&o“The old shafts end in places the miners did not plan for. They left a lantern at the edge of each, and never said why.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor for the distance, Faith for any advancement on the way."
	]
	quest.0C49FE11F89AC5E5.title: "Hollow Hills"
	quest.0C96F45596B0D358.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a backpack from a chest, leather and string. Walk with it, and you carry the storeroom with you."
		""
		"&7&o“The pedlars of the four roads say the heaviest load is the one you left at home.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly: a deeper pack lets you stay out longer, which is how Valor distance is walked."
	]
	quest.0C96F45596B0D358.title: "A Pedlar's Pack"
	quest.0C9933D5EB683ACC.quest_desc: [
		"Deep forest, thick roots, little light. Walk into a dark forest and look around."
	]
	quest.0C9933D5EB683ACC.quest_subtitle: "Wander"
	quest.0C9933D5EB683ACC.title: "Into the Dark Forest"
	quest.0D910C4529DD06CC.quest_desc: [
		"Reach 20,000 EP. In the story, a single naming lifted goblins and wolves far beyond their kin."
	]
	quest.0D910C4529DD06CC.title: "A Named Monster's Strength"
	quest.0E220EAEF0608834.quest_desc: [
		"Sleep in a bed. It sets nothing here (there is no respawn), but skipping the night is the safest way to live long."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Longevity grows with time alive, not with time awake: nights you skip are nights you survive."
	]
	quest.0E220EAEF0608834.title: "A Roof and a Bed"
	quest.0E25F2B8A0455B10.quest_desc: [
		"Gather sixteen blocks of glowstone from the ceilings of the caves. It is brighter than a torch and does not burn."
		""
		"&7&o“Glowstone grows downward from the roof like a lamp someone hung and forgot to light.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.0E25F2B8A0455B10.title: "A Roof of Light"
	quest.0E507B0734BAF632.quest_desc: [
		"Water means fish, clay and a way across. Walk down to a river."
	]
	quest.0E507B0734BAF632.quest_subtitle: "Wander"
	quest.0E507B0734BAF632.title: "Down to the River"
	quest.0F6D40AEB406B8B7.quest_desc: [
		"Carry thirty-two torches. Light your door, your path and every cave mouth you enter: monsters cannot spawn where it is bright."
		""
		"&7&o“In the Realm they say a dark corner is only a monster that has not arrived yet.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Longevity, in the only way that counts: the longer you live, the more days you add."
	]
	quest.0F6D40AEB406B8B7.title: "Chase the Dark Away"
	quest.0FA1FCD9FEF1FAEC.quest_desc: [
		"In the story the orcs are freed from Starved when the Disaster dies (anime season 1, episode 14). The war is decided here: the horde has no king, no hunger driving it, and a very long way to walk home."
	]
	quest.0FA1FCD9FEF1FAEC.quest_subtitle: "Defeat the Orc Disaster"
	quest.0FA1FCD9FEF1FAEC.title: "The Disaster Falls"
	quest.0FFE83FD7094E6BA.quest_desc: [
		"Wear a full set of diamond armour, with a diamond sword and a shield. Iron is good, but the End has no patience for good."
		""
		"&7&o“A plate of diamond turns every wound into a story you will be able to tell.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Craft grows with the diamonds you mined and the anvil work you did; the armour itself is not scored."
	]
	quest.0FFE83FD7094E6BA.title: "Full Plate"
	quest.0FFFE97BBDA23025.quest_desc: [
		"Find a village. Its people are the only other mortals here besides your fellow players."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Order rises when you help them (trade, defend, breed their animals). Killing villagers, golems or traders is the gravest Chaos deed."
	]
	quest.0FFFE97BBDA23025.title: "People of the Realm"
	quest.105B85B97AE88524.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a minecart and lay thirty-two rails. A cart on a line carries ten times what a back can, down a shaft and up again."
		""
		"&7&o“They used ponies once. The ponies preferred the sun, and so did everyone else.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.105B85B97AE88524.title: "Pit Ponies"
	quest.106940F54EF8B23F.quest_desc: [
		"Stand in a crimson forest and a warped forest. Huge fungus for trees, red or blue; one is full of hoglins, the other of endermen."
		""
		"&7&o“The Nether's forests grow from fire and shadow and still manage to look gentle in the dark.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor for the walking; Faith for any advancement on the way."
	]
	quest.106940F54EF8B23F.title: "Forests of Fungus"
	quest.10D40E81D39D1F69.quest_desc: [
		"In the anime Milim finishes Charybdis and Clayman's harlequins are exposed (episode 19); a soul that did Clayman's work and lived is worth more to the Society than one he threw away (our interpretation). The Outcast waits where the road forks south of Tempest's gate and pays in the one coin everybody takes."
		""
		"Return to the Outcast contact."
	]
	quest.10D40E81D39D1F69.quest_subtitle: "Report to the Outcast"
	quest.10D40E81D39D1F69.title: "The Puppet's Pay"
	quest.1167BEB1B24E76ED.quest_desc: [
		"Rimuru was born in the Sealed Cave, where Veldora was held for three hundred years (anime season 1, episode 1). The magicule that leaked out of the seal does not stay quiet (our interpretation): the Supermassive Slime at the altar is what is left of it. Anyone may fight it, whatever road they walk."
		""
		"Stand in the cave's antechamber and claim the reward to wake it. It must be started within 96 blocks of the altar."
	]
	quest.1167BEB1B24E76ED.quest_subtitle: "Veldora's leftovers (optional)"
	quest.1167BEB1B24E76ED.title: "The Cave Stirs"
	quest.12C27DC231767DC2.quest_desc: [
		"Find the old goblin village north-west of Tempest, where Rigurd's tribe hid from the direwolves before the slime came."
	]
	quest.12C27DC231767DC2.title: "Rigurd's Tribe"
	quest.1351A538F40C5424.quest_desc: [
		"Find a Nether fortress. Blazes and wither skeletons guard it."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor: each new kind of foe you slay adds 4 Valor karma, so fortress dwellers are worth hunting."
	]
	quest.1351A538F40C5424.title: "Fortress"
	quest.144A3DF14FC2676F.quest_desc: [
		"Naming is how Rimuru lifted goblins and wolves far above their kin, and it left him drained for days. A monster only accepts a name when it submits to you (tamed, subdued, or loyal), and you need enough EP to pay for it. The book detects the naming itself, whoever you name."
	]
	quest.144A3DF14FC2676F.title: "From Now On, Your Name Is..."
	quest.146D12495A6AF61B.quest_desc: [
		"Scoop a bucket of lava from a deep pool: wear armour, be careful, keep a bucket of water in the other hand."
		""
		"&7&o“A man who has carried lava in his hands will say, truthfully, that he is not afraid of the dark.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Faith for the advancement (+2)."
	]
	quest.146D12495A6AF61B.title: "A Bucket of Fire"
	quest.14DA7048CD6D4A6B.quest_desc: [
		"Find a trail ruin: broken walls half-buried in the earth, with cracked clay and mud bricks. Dig carefully and bring a brush."
		""
		"&7&o“Whoever walked these trails left their pottery behind. Fifty generations on, someone is still sweeping it.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor for the ground covered."
	]
	quest.14DA7048CD6D4A6B.title: "Trails Under the Grass"
	quest.152AEAE80A21A4C2.quest_desc: [
		"Use a brewing stand ten times. Each pass of a bottle through it counts: water, then a base, then the potion you wanted."
		""
		"&7&o“The first potion is an accident. The tenth is a recipe. After that it is a life's work.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Faith: every use of a brewing stand adds a little (0.5 each)."
	]
	quest.152AEAE80A21A4C2.title: "Many Brews"
	quest.15545C55B1BB168E.quest_desc: [
		"Bake two pumpkin pies, then a cake, and eat a slice of it. Share the rest with whoever is nearby."
		""
		"&7&o“A cake in the Realm is never baked for one person; that is how you can tell it was meant.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly: this is a celebration, and the Realm keeps no ledger for those."
	]
	quest.15545C55B1BB168E.title: "Cake Day"
	quest.157D58DC52006FFD.quest_desc: [
		"Rigurd's tribe left its old village for Tempest, and the huts in the north-west stand empty. That makes them a fine place to meet someone who should not be seen at a goblin fire: the Horde's envoy (our interpretation). He wants a strong blade, and he already knows yours."
		""
		"Walk the abandoned goblin village and wait for him."
	]
	quest.157D58DC52006FFD.quest_subtitle: "Empty huts, a waiting stranger"
	quest.157D58DC52006FFD.title: "The Horde's Envoy"
	quest.1585311527965ABC.quest_desc: [
		"The marsh is quiet. In the story the Orc Disaster's death ends the war and the lizardmen, goblins, ogres and orcs of the forest sit down at one table (anime season 1, episode 15). Whichever road you took, the forest knows who was at the front of the war."
		""
		"Claim the reward to close the act: it records Act III and applies its reputation (light: Lizardmen +20, Tempest +10; dark: Orc Horde +40, Lizardmen -20). The next chapter is the calamity on the lake."
	]
	quest.1585311527965ABC.quest_subtitle: "Act III"
	quest.1585311527965ABC.title: "The Orc War"
	quest.16C682117AAF591D.quest_desc: [
		"Canon says three days by wolf and two months on foot, and the road north has no inns. Pack food, a good pickaxe and torches before you leave the forest: 16 cooked beef, an iron pickaxe and 32 torches in your inventory."
	]
	quest.16C682117AAF591D.title: "Provisions for the Road"
	quest.176D0BD7DFECF684.quest_desc: [
		"Trade with a villager."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Order: every trade adds Order karma. Souls with strong Order lean towards Blumund and the Church in the next life."
	]
	quest.176D0BD7DFECF684.title: "A Fair Deal"
	quest.177FAA70EB81D656.quest_desc: [
		"Carry three golden apples: eight gold ingots each, and a wound that would have ended you becomes a long afternoon."
		""
		"&7&o“The old rule of the Realm: bring more food than you plan to eat, and more courage than you plan to need.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.177FAA70EB81D656.title: "Apples of Gold"
	quest.17D2C8763547C148.quest_desc: [
		"Defend a village from a raid and win. Careful: walking into a village with Bad Omen BRINGS the raid on it, which counts as a dark deed."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Order +30 for every raid won; Chaos +3 for every raid you started. Win what you start."
	]
	quest.17D2C8763547C148.title: "Hero of the Village"
	quest.1805CB3013712C63.quest_desc: [
		"Mine diamonds. Deepslate diamonds count as much as the shallow kind."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Craft: every diamond you mine adds Craft karma (2 per ore)."
	]
	quest.1805CB3013712C63.title: "Diamonds"
	quest.1816F54043A80DF7.quest_desc: [
		"Craft four lanterns from torches and iron nuggets, and hang them over the door and along the yard wall."
		""
		"&7&o“At dusk the lamplighter of Wayfarer's Rest walks the square, and the Realm seems a little less large.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.1816F54043A80DF7.title: "Lamplighter"
	quest.181ABFB92A6CF8C1.quest_desc: [
		"Pour water over still lava until it turns to obsidian, and mine ten blocks with a diamond pickaxe. This is the stone a Nether portal is made of."
		""
		"&7&o“Obsidian is born when two things that should destroy each other are made to meet. The Realm's smiths say it is the only honest alloy.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Faith for the advancement (+2). It is also the road to chapter 0's Mortal Nether (+20 Valor)."
	]
	quest.181ABFB92A6CF8C1.title: "Cooled by Water"
	quest.184ED3B4C58EB59C.quest_desc: [
		"Before the ogres and before the Orc Lord, the Orc Horde was only rumour on the wind. Its buyers pay for strength they can use: direwolf pelts and proof that you do not flinch (our interpretation, foreshadowing the Orc War, anime season 1, episode 10)."
		""
		"Kill eight direwolves. Where the light road tames the pack, the dark road thins it."
	]
	quest.184ED3B4C58EB59C.quest_subtitle: "Pelts for the Horde"
	quest.184ED3B4C58EB59C.title: "The Cull"
	quest.189621086A58B950.quest_desc: [
		"Find an ocean monument and slay its Elder Guardian. Bring milk, doors or a lot of air."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor +50 and a great foe: it counts towards the Legend tier."
	]
	quest.189621086A58B950.title: "The Drowned Temple"
	quest.18A697DC12B0852B.quest_desc: [
		"In the story Milim ends Charybdis and spares Phobio, the beast prince it possessed (anime season 1, episode 19). Here the ending is yours. When it falls the water goes still."
	]
	quest.18A697DC12B0852B.quest_subtitle: "Defeat Charybdis"
	quest.18A697DC12B0852B.title: "The Whirlpool Calamity"
	quest.18E68A4477A5FF08.quest_desc: [
		"Ferment two spider eyes: a spider eye, brown mushroom and sugar make the key ingredient of weakness, slowness and harming."
		""
		"&7&o“Not every potion is to be drunk. Some are for the second, less polite part of the conversation.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Faith for the brews (see Many Brews)."
	]
	quest.18E68A4477A5FF08.title: "Dark Chemistry"
	quest.18F996B57F79B262.quest_desc: [
		"A besieged people eat first and fight second. The lizardmen have fish but little else; Rimuru sent supplies. Hand in 24 cooked cod and 16 bread to their storehouse."
	]
	quest.18F996B57F79B262.title: "Rations for the Lizardmen"
	quest.1901591983305FCD.quest_desc: [
		"Sawing planks by hand slows a whole town down. Craft a woodcutter (planks and an iron ingot) and bring it to the lumber yard, where the half-built houses wait for boards."
	]
	quest.1901591983305FCD.title: "A Woodcutter for the Lumber Yard"
	quest.1A805F105A11A42A.quest_desc: [
		"Every kill adds to your EP. Reach 1,000, the point where the world stops treating you as ordinary and calls you D-Class."
	]
	quest.1A805F105A11A42A.title: "Just an Average Monster"
	quest.1A837B4EC88D3394.quest_desc: [
		"When the wolves are gone, the ants and spiders crawl in from the undergrowth. Hakurou says a town that cannot watch its own fields does not deserve them. Kill six giant ants and three black spiders."
	]
	quest.1A837B4EC88D3394.title: "Pests of the Forest"
	quest.1B936E59B637BCED.quest_desc: [
		"Reach 100,000 EP (Special-A Class): a disaster the world has to plan around."
	]
	quest.1B936E59B637BCED.title: "Calamity-Class"
	quest.1BDC7581ED18FA26.quest_desc: [
		"Mine ancient debris in the Mortal Nether and forge a netherite ingot."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Craft: every block of ancient debris adds 5 Craft karma."
	]
	quest.1BDC7581ED18FA26.title: "Ancient Debris"
	quest.1BEAF15E9E6E9890.quest_desc: [
		"Gabiru has sworn to hold the lake against the orcs, and the Horde knows it (anime season 1, episodes 11-12). A besieged people that is hit from inside its own caverns breaks faster than one that is hit from the marsh. Go to the caverns the lizardmen hold and cut down twelve of them."
		""
		"&6Why it matters:&r Act III costs a dark soul the lizardmen's goodwill (Lizardmen -20) and wins the Horde's (Orc Horde +40)."
	]
	quest.1BEAF15E9E6E9890.quest_subtitle: "Betray the lizardmen"
	quest.1BEAF15E9E6E9890.title: "Raid the Caverns"
	quest.1C3E20B311E1AB34.quest_desc: [
		"Talk to ten villagers: right-click, listen to the grunt, and look at what they will sell. Every trade begins as a greeting."
		""
		"&7&o“A villager will not say a word you can understand, but the cartographer has a way of saying it with real feeling.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly: trades are Order, and a greeting is the road to one."
	]
	quest.1C3E20B311E1AB34.title: "Good Morning"
	quest.1C5D6216B7FD58CF.quest_desc: [
		"Enchant 10 items."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Faith: 2 karma per enchantment."
	]
	quest.1C5D6216B7FD58CF.title: "Scholar"
	quest.1C7A1C8BD2A8FE30.quest_desc: [
		"Hold thirty-two emeralds from your trades. Sell what you grow, mine or cook, and never take more than a fair price."
		""
		"&7&o“In the Realm a purse never fills by itself. It is filled by people who were glad to see you.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Order: each trade is +1, and the first twenty-five trades count the most."
	]
	quest.1C7A1C8BD2A8FE30.title: "A Heavy Purse"
	quest.1C877BA54AD9295D.quest_desc: [
		"A cold forge makes no iron. Hand in 12 coal."
	]
	quest.1C877BA54AD9295D.quest_subtitle: "Gather"
	quest.1C877BA54AD9295D.title: "A Day's Fuel"
	quest.1D03190909C19A0D.quest_desc: [
		"Find the village bell and ring it once. A bell calls the villagers to shelter: use it for a good reason only."
		""
		"&7&o“The bell is the one voice a whole village obeys at the same moment.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly: ringing it for a raid is just a warning, and the raid, if you bring it, is a Chaos deed."
	]
	quest.1D03190909C19A0D.title: "Ring the Bell"
	quest.1D2BA21736C69E22.quest_desc: [
		"A horde follows hunger, and hunger follows the strongest mouth. Geld is a king because he ate his rivals; the only way to the Horde's crown is to eat him in turn (our interpretation: in the anime the Disaster itself is devoured by Rimuru, episode 14). Anyone may fight him, whatever road they walk."
		""
		"Stand in the orc camp itself and claim the reward to start the fight. He summons the horde at 60% health and goes into a frenzy at 30%."
		""
		"&6If the call fails&r (the Orc Lord is already out, or resting: 24 hours, or you are more than 96 blocks from the camp's centre), find the camp with /ttl landmark where orc_camp and type /ttl story fight orc_lord there."
	]
	quest.1D2BA21736C69E22.quest_subtitle: "Begin the fight"
	quest.1D2BA21736C69E22.title: "Take the Horde"
	quest.1D3D81B3B457597B.quest_desc: [
		"Spiders drop from the ceiling of every cave. Kill six, and keep their string for later."
	]
	quest.1D3D81B3B457597B.quest_subtitle: "Hunt"
	quest.1D3D81B3B457597B.title: "Eight Legs Too Many"
	quest.1DD21FE7DFA820E5.quest_desc: [
		"Find an abandoned mineshaft: rotten timbers, cobwebs and chests nobody came back for. Carry torches and do not mind the spiders."
		""
		"&7&o“Nobody remembers who dug the old shafts. The oldest miner in Wayfarer's Rest says they were there when the Realm was made, and so was he.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor for the distance travelled to find one."
	]
	quest.1DD21FE7DFA820E5.title: "Old Shafts"
	quest.1E1AD89FFD572291.quest_desc: [
		"Stay alive for 30 days (10 hours of play)."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Longevity: 30 days is the least a soul needs to be judged a Legend."
	]
	quest.1E1AD89FFD572291.title: "A Full Life"
	quest.1E5B98A6CFF7815D.quest_desc: [
		"Schematics teach smiths to make katana, swords and armour; the schematic is used up and the recipe stays. Craft a smithing bench to work from. If you already built one for Kaijin in Tempest, the same bench counts."
	]
	quest.1E5B98A6CFF7815D.title: "A Smith's Bench"
	quest.1F70B3D16096430C.quest_desc: [
		"Tempest's allies gathered at the water while Vesta's full potions came off the bench (anime season 1, episode 17). A shore camp has to be fed and mended before anything rises out of the lake."
		""
		"Walk to the lake's western shore, where the forest ends, and hand in six low potions for the line."
	]
	quest.1F70B3D16096430C.quest_subtitle: "Potions for the line"
	quest.1F70B3D16096430C.title: "The Shore Camp"
	quest.1F7212F6209FDAB3.quest_desc: [
		"Gobta is the hobgoblin who volunteers first, rides a wolf badly and boasts well. Find him at the goblins' campfire, south of Rigurd's hut."
	]
	quest.1F7212F6209FDAB3.title: "Gobta, Wolf Rider"
	quest.1F9294FDE0A06C93.quest_desc: [
		"Put a lightning rod over a villager's house and let a thunderstorm come: a struck villager turns into a witch, but a rod catches the bolt first."
		""
		"&7&o“Nobody in the village can say who put the rod up. They only say the storm has not hurt them since.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Faith for the advancement (+2), and Order: a protected village is a better one."
	]
	quest.1F9294FDE0A06C93.title: "Surge Protector"
	quest.2132F3CD7B78FC48.quest_desc: [
		"Fill an iron bucket with water. Dig a well in the yard: water beats fire, feeds crops and breaks a long fall."
		""
		"&7&o“A village without a well is a village waiting for a fire.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.2132F3CD7B78FC48.title: "A Well in the Yard"
	quest.219098709232BE9A.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a campfire: three sticks, coal or charcoal and three logs. Cook on it, sit by it, and let it show the way home."
		""
		"&7&o“A hearth makes a house; walls are only what keeps the draught off it.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.219098709232BE9A.title: "The Hearth"
	quest.21B1F1A48AFB857E.quest_desc: [
		"West of the plaza stands the forge hall: three chimneys, copper roofs, cogs on the walls, an open front you can walk into. Dwargon makes weapons here for the whole continent."
	]
	quest.21B1F1A48AFB857E.title: "The Great Forge Hall"
	quest.21C4013E065B227E.quest_desc: [
		"Till the soil next to water, plant your seed and harvest twenty-four wheat. A well-watered plot is all a good crop asks."
		""
		"&7&o“The first loaf you eat from your own field tastes of nothing special, and nothing else will ever taste as good.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.21C4013E065B227E.title: "First Harvest"
	quest.223D5908F2639057.quest_desc: [
		"Fence a few chickens in with wheat seeds and gather twelve eggs. Eggs bake, trade and breed more hens."
		""
		"&7&o“A morning without the crow of a rooster is a morning the Realm did not quite mean to have.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly: but a flock that grows is animals bred (Order), if you breed it."
	]
	quest.223D5908F2639057.title: "A Hen-House"
	quest.22BF60FD6B9D6839.quest_desc: [
		"Gazel sat silent when you knelt, and a king who stays silent is still counting. Word of an Oath sworn in the forest has reached the white gate (Act I is behind you), and the court has noticed who walks its stair."
		""
		"Walk back up to the royal terrace, where the guards now step aside."
	]
	quest.22BF60FD6B9D6839.quest_subtitle: "Act II begins"
	quest.22BF60FD6B9D6839.title: "The King Looks Up"
	quest.2327C864EFF03C30.quest_desc: [
		"Smelt eight copper ingots. It is soft and bright and turns green, but it makes spyglasses, lightning rods and good roofs."
		""
		"&7&o“The coppersmiths of the Realm say the metal remembers every rain that ever fell on it.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.2327C864EFF03C30.title: "Green Metal"
	quest.23B0B39D449831F2.quest_desc: [
		"In the story Kaijin leaves Dwargon for Tempest under the King's sentence (anime season 1, episode 5). Here the King, having tested what stands behind Tempest, lets the smiths trade across the border: iron and silver in one direction, finished steel in the other."
		""
		"Bring Kaijin the first shipment, sixteen iron ingots and four silver ingots, in his smithy."
	]
	quest.23B0B39D449831F2.quest_subtitle: "Kaijin walks free (our interpretation)"
	quest.23B0B39D449831F2.title: "A Pact of Smiths"
	quest.23ED2FA8FF8BE68A.quest_desc: [
		"Find a bee nest in a flower forest or meadow and harvest a bottle of honey: put a campfire under the nest so the bees stay calm."
		""
		"&7&o“The bees do not care what you want, only whether you smell of smoke.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Faith for the advancement (+2)."
	]
	quest.23ED2FA8FF8BE68A.title: "The Bee-Keeper"
	quest.24A79CFC701B4EB8.quest_desc: [
		"Benimaru, Shuna, Shion, Souei, Hakurou and Kurobe sat at this long table when Rimuru named them, and the first plans against the coming trouble were made here. Walk in and take your seat on the benches."
	]
	quest.24A79CFC701B4EB8.title: "The Council Longhouse"
	quest.259326FA8E3E9655.quest_desc: [
		"Slay the rarer things of the Overworld: an enderman, a witch and a phantom."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor: three more kinds of foe, 4 Valor karma each."
	]
	quest.259326FA8E3E9655.title: "Strange Foes"
	quest.25E18FB809A0CA5D.quest_desc: [
		"Make a banner at a loom and work it three times: a pattern, a colour, a device. Hang it over your gate."
		""
		"&7&o“A banner says who you are before you open your mouth, which is why so few are ever lowered.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.25E18FB809A0CA5D.title: "Heraldry"
	quest.26616A4D8CE7AC47.quest_desc: [
		"Craft Eyes of Ender. Throw one and follow it to the stronghold."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Each step towards the End is a step towards a Legend's soul: a Legend needs at least one great foe slain."
	]
	quest.26616A4D8CE7AC47.title: "Eyes of Ender"
	quest.26A6D1053EDA56FF.quest_desc: [
		"The forge hall on the plaza and the engineers' workshop on the east side keep the plans of Dwargon's first technology tier on their walls. Nobody counts the paper in a smith's trash, and nobody guards what everyone already sees. Visit both halls and copy what you can: eight sheets of paper for the broker."
		""
		"&6Why it matters:&r Act II costs a dark soul Dwargon -20 and gives Outcast Society +10. The quiet way spends nothing more."
	]
	quest.26A6D1053EDA56FF.quest_subtitle: "The quiet way"
	quest.26A6D1053EDA56FF.title: "Steal the Schematics"
	quest.26F513965BD87791.quest_desc: [
		"The orcs that were left were never the enemy: they were starving, and the hunger was a king's skill, not theirs. In the story the freed orcs join the lizardmen and the goblins in the Jura alliance (anime season 1, episode 15). Here the survivors are fed at the camp, and the ones who choose to stay take Tempest's name."
		""
		"Stand in the camp and hand in twenty-four baked potatoes. The claim records that the orcs joined Tempest."
	]
	quest.26F513965BD87791.quest_subtitle: "They join Tempest (our interpretation)"
	quest.26F513965BD87791.title: "Spare the Orcs"
	quest.27035168A6DEED93.quest_desc: [
		"Walk the streets of early Tempest, the town Rimuru built for goblins and direwolves. Goblins, wolves, dwarves and kijin live side by side here; behave like a guest."
	]
	quest.27035168A6DEED93.title: "The Town of Monsters"
	quest.273C7127B5C24215.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a smoker. It cooks meat and fish twice as fast as a furnace, which is a fine thing when the night is long."
		""
		"&7&o“A smokehouse is slow work for hungry people, and so every winter tale of the Realm is set in one.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.273C7127B5C24215.title: "The Smokehouse"
	quest.279E2D0B9F04D34D.quest_desc: [
		"Geld waits at the heart of the horde, and nothing the forest has can stop him except a few who dare to meet him on his own ground (anime season 1, episode 13). The lizardmen hold the marsh while you do. Anyone may fight him, whatever road they walk."
		""
		"Stand in the orc camp itself and claim the reward to start the fight. He summons the horde at 60% health and goes into a frenzy at 30%. Bring a party."
		""
		"&6If the call fails&r (the Orc Lord is already out, or resting: 24 hours, or you are more than 96 blocks from the camp's centre), find the camp with /ttl landmark where orc_camp and type /ttl story fight orc_lord there."
	]
	quest.279E2D0B9F04D34D.quest_subtitle: "Begin the fight"
	quest.279E2D0B9F04D34D.title: "Face the Orc Lord"
	quest.2838EEA8E8718D5C.quest_desc: [
		"The lake is calm again. In the story the victory is celebrated in Tempest, and then Yuuki walks in with a warning about Shizu's students (anime season 1, episode 20). Whichever road you took, the water gave something up: the forest's strongest now know what you are."
		""
		"Claim the reward to close the act: it records Act IV and applies its reputation (light: Tempest +15; dark: Outcast Society +20)."
	]
	quest.2838EEA8E8718D5C.quest_subtitle: "Act IV"
	quest.2838EEA8E8718D5C.title: "Calamity"
	quest.283DBEA71CB9C9E6.quest_desc: [
		"Punch a tree until it gives, turn the logs into planks and the planks into eight sticks. Nothing here is built without them."
		""
		"&7&o“Every road in the Realm began with a splinter in somebody's palm.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly. A soul that survives the first hour is already counting days."
	]
	quest.283DBEA71CB9C9E6.quest_subtitle: "Gather sticks"
	quest.283DBEA71CB9C9E6.title: "Bare Hands"
	quest.287D2F8E30D91857.quest_desc: [
		"Whichever way you took the kingdom's measure, it must be told to someone who pays for it. The Outcast waits where the road forks south of Tempest's gate, and you had better leave Dwargon before the guards remember your face."
		""
		"Return to the Outcast contact on the south road."
	]
	quest.287D2F8E30D91857.quest_subtitle: "Report to the Outcast"
	quest.287D2F8E30D91857.title: "The Spoils"
	quest.28B77958A89D5BEA.quest_desc: [
		"Reach 3,000 EP (C-Class). A named goblin or wolf is stronger than most travellers; you should not trail behind them."
	]
	quest.28B77958A89D5BEA.title: "Fit for a Named Pack"
	quest.28ECD42F864E39EB.quest_desc: [
		"Find a ruined portal: a broken frame of obsidian with a chest nearby. Someone started a journey here and did not finish it."
		""
		"&7&o“The villagers do not go near them. They say a half-opened door lets in more than the draught.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor for the ground covered."
	]
	quest.28ECD42F864E39EB.title: "A Gate Nobody Lit"
	quest.28F253E6D9F16E29.quest_desc: [
		"Stand in a forest, a taiga and a swamp. In the large biomes they are far apart: plan the journey, pack food and mark your route."
		""
		"&7&o“The three greens of the Realm have never agreed on what the weather ought to be.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor for the ground covered, Faith for any advancement on the way."
	]
	quest.28F253E6D9F16E29.title: "The Green Lands"
	quest.295AA61F9C55A114.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a piece of iron armour."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Faith for the advancement; Craft grows with the work behind it."
	]
	quest.295AA61F9C55A114.title: "Suit Up"
	quest.29D5C5EA2B017525.quest_desc: [
		"In the story Geld devours his master Gelmud and the dead of the battlefield and rises again as the Orc Disaster, a catastrophe no one in the forest can face alone (anime season 1, episode 14). The war is not won until he is."
		""
		"Stand on the battlefield and claim the reward to start the final battle. The Disaster is a harder fight than the Lord: more health, a starving horde behind him, and a frenzy at 30% health."
		""
		"&6If the call fails&r (the Disaster is already out, or resting: 48 hours), type /ttl story fight orc_disaster at the battlefield."
	]
	quest.29D5C5EA2B017525.quest_subtitle: "Begin the last battle"
	quest.29D5C5EA2B017525.title: "The One Who Devours All"
	quest.2AFA8C648E4A5880.quest_desc: [
		"Crack open an amethyst geode and take eight shards. Do not let it ring: the crystals chime when anyone steps near."
		""
		"&7&o“Amethyst does not shine so much as hum, in a pitch only a trained miner can hear.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.2AFA8C648E4A5880.title: "A Crystal Cave"
	quest.2C15A112C215C57B.quest_desc: [
		"Mine thirty-two nether quartz from the wastes. It makes comparators, daylight sensors and the whitest blocks the Realm has."
		""
		"&7&o“The quartz is the only thing in the Nether you would want to bring home.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.2C15A112C215C57B.title: "White Stone, Red Hell"
	quest.2C81A67626C6E40E.quest_desc: [
		"Keep fighting. Resistances finish forming after enough punishment, and then a wolf's bite or a spider's fang is shrugged off. Learn Physical Attack Resistance fully."
	]
	quest.2C81A67626C6E40E.title: "Learnt the Hard Way"
	quest.2CE61123525F4E23.quest_desc: [
		"Stock eight blaze powder (it fuels the stand) and twelve glass bottles. A brewer who has to stop to craft his bottles has already lost the afternoon."
		""
		"&7&o“Brewers say the powder is the only part of a blaze worth keeping, and the blaze would probably agree.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly: the brews are, a little at a time."
	]
	quest.2CE61123525F4E23.title: "Powder and Glass"
	quest.2D0434A6C1F58EC6.quest_desc: [
		"Hills, coast, wreck, trail, tower and a broken gate. You have walked a good part of the Realm. Tick it off when you can name every place you have been; The Ledger (chapter 0j) counts it as a way of life."
		""
		"&7&o“The map-seller at the crossroads says the best map is the one you could draw from memory with your eyes shut.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor: ground explored is scored by the squares you entered, not by this milestone."
	]
	quest.2D0434A6C1F58EC6.quest_subtitle: "The exploration milestone"
	quest.2D0434A6C1F58EC6.title: "Cartographer's Pride"
	quest.2D5BB123175ECA77.quest_desc: [
		"Find trial chambers beneath the ground and slay a breeze."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor: the breeze is one more kind of foe."
	]
	quest.2D5BB123175ECA77.title: "Trial Chambers"
	quest.2DB50F1703D405E4.quest_desc: [
		"Stand in a meadow, on a windswept hill and on a snowy slope. Up here the wind carries the bells of faraway flocks."
		""
		"&7&o“Shepherds of the high country do not speak much. The wind does it for them.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor for the ground covered."
	]
	quest.2DB50F1703D405E4.title: "The High Country"
	quest.2F2C876EEE6CAF98.quest_desc: [
		"A hearth, windows, a full storeroom, a well, a wall and beds for guests. This is a homestead. Tick it off when you are proud of it: it counts as one of the ways of life that The Ledger (chapter 0j) adds up."
		""
		"&7&o“They will tell a long tale about you one day. It will start, as most do, at a door with a lamp over it.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Longevity and calm: a soul that builds a home is a soul that stays alive to use it."
	]
	quest.2F2C876EEE6CAF98.quest_subtitle: "The homestead milestone"
	quest.2F2C876EEE6CAF98.title: "Home Fires"
	quest.2F5E407CC816055C.quest_desc: [
		"After the dragon falls a gateway opens at the edge of the main island. Throw an ender pearl through it and see where the End goes."
		""
		"&7&o“The main island is only the doorstep of the End. The rest is a very long yard.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Faith for the advancement (+2)."
	]
	quest.2F5E407CC816055C.title: "Beyond the Island"
	quest.3050EAF03EB34E0A.quest_desc: [
		"Gather sixteen cobblestone walls and ring your yard. Zombies cannot jump a wall of this height; creepers, alas, do not care."
		""
		"&7&o“A low wall will not stop a siege, but it tells a stranger that someone lives here.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.3050EAF03EB34E0A.title: "A Wall Against the Wolves"
	quest.30E565DAB9906323.quest_desc: [
		"The first house on the west side of the forge street was Kaijin's before King Gazel exiled him after a sham trial. His anvil, his blast furnace and his lava cauldron are still where he left them. Stand in his forge."
	]
	quest.30E565DAB9906323.title: "Kaijin's Old Smithy"
	quest.314ED94175235B90.quest_desc: [
		"They know your face, your prices and which door you knock on. You gave a village's people work and a village's traders fair custom. Tick it off when you would be missed; The Ledger (chapter 0j) counts it as a way of life."
		""
		"&7&o“On market days they save you a stool. The stool is the highest honour the Realm has.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Order: this is what the trade count in your life record is made of."
	]
	quest.314ED94175235B90.quest_subtitle: "The villages milestone"
	quest.314ED94175235B90.title: "Friend of the Hamlet"
	quest.315BB043D91F9146.quest_desc: [
		"A word of warning, not a task. Slaying villagers, iron golems, wandering traders or other players, and starting raids, are dark deeds. A soul whose Chaos outweighs its Order is reborn Fallen, and dark races (orcs, ghouls, daemons, vampires) join its offers. Nothing is ever taken away, but the Voice of the World remembers."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Chaos counts half towards the tier: the dark path climbs, but slower than good deeds."
	]
	quest.315BB043D91F9146.title: "The Other Road"
	quest.3192ECC2F5206C40.quest_desc: [
		"The first thing the slime learned to do was to see without eyes: Magic Sense reads the magicules around you. Learn it (any way the world allows). Skills are never handed out by this book."
	]
	quest.3192ECC2F5206C40.title: "Magic Sense"
	quest.32DDE3E79622B19D.quest_desc: [
		"Plant carrots and potatoes (villages grow them, zombies carry them) and bring in sixteen of each."
		""
		"&7&o“The villagers keep a few crops back as seed corn, and a fool who steals it is a fool who starves.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly. Do not steal from a village's farms: nothing here is taken for you."
	]
	quest.32DDE3E79622B19D.title: "Roots and Tubers"
	quest.335512BF337D39FE.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a carved pumpkin and fill a water bucket. Wear the pumpkin and endermen will ignore your face; stand in the water and they cannot reach you."
		""
		"&7&o“The hunters' oldest trick is also the silliest-looking, and it has kept more of them alive than any sword.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.335512BF337D39FE.title: "The Pumpkin and the Pail"
	quest.336C7509DDEA2416.quest_desc: [
		"After the battle the town celebrates: Carrion agrees to a non-aggression pact, the harlequins are exposed as Clayman's, and the victory is feasted before Yuuki arrives (anime season 1, episodes 19-20). Everyone who fought is owed a seat at the fire."
		""
		"Take eight cooked cod to the green and eat with the people you defended."
	]
	quest.336C7509DDEA2416.quest_subtitle: "Tempest celebrates"
	quest.336C7509DDEA2416.title: "The Victory Feast"
	quest.33773FD7757DFBC8.quest_desc: [
		"Gabiru swears to stand with Tempest against the horde. In the story he is proud, and not easy to fight beside: his warriors will hold the lake while the forest's army meets the orcs. The book cannot detect an alliance, so this is a promise you make yourself. Tick it when you stand with them."
	]
	quest.33773FD7757DFBC8.title: "The Lizardmen's Alliance"
	quest.33FCE563EA7EA5CF.quest_desc: [
		"The dead walk when the sun goes down. Put ten zombies back in the ground and sleep better."
	]
	quest.33FCE563EA7EA5CF.quest_subtitle: "Hunt"
	quest.33FCE563EA7EA5CF.title: "Clear the Night"
	quest.34884FFE5F8393B9.quest_desc: [
		"Find a shipwreck and an underwater ruin. Bring a boat, water breathing if you can, and a bucket to clear the sand."
		""
		"&7&o“Some wrecks are older than any harbour. The sea rarely gives a reason, only a chest.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor for the ground covered, Faith for any advancement."
	]
	quest.34884FFE5F8393B9.title: "Wrecks and Ruins"
	quest.358E4EA8FE88E607.quest_desc: [
		"A king does not meet a nobody. Reach 6,000 EP (B-Class): a monster the guards would hesitate to turn away."
	]
	quest.358E4EA8FE88E607.title: "B-Class"
	quest.360847E3AB660F98.quest_desc: [
		"Milk a cow into an iron bucket. Milk clears every sickness a bad potion or a spider could give you."
		""
		"&7&o“Ask a farm girl what she loves most about cows and she will say it is how patient they are with fools.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.360847E3AB660F98.title: "Fresh Milk"
	quest.36CA793DF8F0E397.quest_desc: [
		"Bake twelve loaves of bread: three wheat each, one bench. Bread is the cheapest food you can carry far."
		""
		"&7&o“The baker of Wayfarer's Rest is up before the bell, and the bell is up before the sun.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.36CA793DF8F0E397.title: "The Baker's Hour"
	quest.37100E5E69336D70.quest_desc: [
		"A slime the size of a house, and it splits when it is hurt. Bring a party, bring fire, and do not stand still."
	]
	quest.37100E5E69336D70.quest_subtitle: "Defeat the Supermassive Slime (optional)"
	quest.37100E5E69336D70.title: "What the Seal Left"
	quest.3777A86A848909DD.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a composter, a lectern, a loom and a grindstone. An unemployed villager picks a job when it finds the right block: a farmer, a librarian, a shepherd, a toolsmith."
		""
		"&7&o“A village's whole wealth is the number of its hands that have something to do.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Order: a villager given work is a village that can trade (each trade adds +1)."
	]
	quest.3777A86A848909DD.title: "A Trade for Everyone"
	quest.384C1793A5436F8A.quest_desc: [
		"Apples, a pumpkin and a pail, stone, plate, an anvil-mended kit and a bow. Tick it off when you would walk into the End with all of it on your back. Chapter 0 asks for the portal and the dragon; this checklist only asks that you come ready. The Ledger (chapter 0j) counts it as a way of life."
		""
		"&7&o“On the evening before a long journey the Realm says nothing. It only leaves the porch light on.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor: +30 once for reaching the Mortal End, +120 and a great foe for the dragon; this milestone only says you prepared."
	]
	quest.384C1793A5436F8A.quest_subtitle: "The preparation milestone"
	quest.384C1793A5436F8A.title: "The Dragon's Eve"
	quest.39605C1707E5BD4A.quest_desc: [
		"Stand on a beach and in the open ocean. Salt air, kelp and a very long way to anywhere else."
		""
		"&7&o“Fishers hold that the sea has a memory and a temper and that only one of the two can be bargained with.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor for the ground covered."
	]
	quest.39605C1707E5BD4A.title: "Salt and Sand"
	quest.397ABE2F023AD1E0.quest_desc: [
		"Gather six chorus fruits and two chorus flowers. Eat a fruit and you are thrown a short way; plant a flower and it grows like nothing else."
		""
		"&7&o“The chorus plants hum when you cross them. The Realm calls it singing; the Realm is polite.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.397ABE2F023AD1E0.title: "A Garden of Chorus"
	quest.3CBF4118CD1C5AF7.quest_desc: [
		"The houses have doors, the store is full, the forge is lit and the looms run. The first night raid broke on the palisade. Rimuru calls it a town, and a town is asked where it stands: the road south of the gate splits in two (the Crossroads chapter). The road north to Dwargon, and east to Lake Siss, opens after that. This is a milestone: tick it off when you are ready to look beyond the forest."
	]
	quest.3CBF4118CD1C5AF7.quest_subtitle: "A town, not a camp"
	quest.3CBF4118CD1C5AF7.title: "Tempest Stands"
	quest.3D024E08F02CAA7A.quest_desc: [
		"Slay the dragon of the Mortal End. The killing blow is what counts. Whatever happens next, this deed follows your soul into the next life."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor +120 and a great foe: the Legend tier needs at least one great foe slain, with 1000 karma and 30 days lived."
	]
	quest.3D024E08F02CAA7A.title: "The Mortal Dragon"
	quest.3D14EC5F5890B8B5.quest_desc: [
		"In the story it began with a name: Rimuru named the goblins and the direwolves, and the naming bound giver and given alike (anime season 1, episodes 2-3). Tempest keeps that idea. Words said at the south gate stay said."
		""
		"Stand at the fork south of the gate, then claim the reward: it opens the Oath menu (the same menu opens if you talk to Rigurd, or type /ttl story oath). Two roads: the light one, with Rigurd's folk, or the dark one, with the Outcasts and the Orc Horde. In a party the leader swears and the whole party is bound with them. The choice is not undone by wishing: only a later Atonement or Corruption can turn you, once."
		""
		"&6Why it matters:&r the light Oath gives Tempest +20; the dark Oath gives Outcast Society +20 and Orc Horde +15 and costs Tempest 20. Both lanes below are full quest lines of the same size."
	]
	quest.3D14EC5F5890B8B5.quest_subtitle: "Swear the Oath"
	quest.3D14EC5F5890B8B5.title: "Crossroads"
	quest.3D866D739BE52404.quest_desc: [
		"Find a desert pyramid and a jungle temple. Tread carefully: both hold treasure and both hold a trap for those who forget to look down."
		""
		"&7&o“Neither was built for pilgrims. Both were built so that someone, once, would not have to be found.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor for the ground covered; Faith for any advancement."
	]
	quest.3D866D739BE52404.title: "Temples in the Sand"
	quest.3DDBBA44FD7AC19F.quest_desc: [
		"Find a mushroom island, the rarest land in the realm."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor for the distance travelled; a long road is a brave road."
	]
	quest.3DDBBA44FD7AC19F.title: "Far Shores"
	quest.3E112E381ADA60B4.quest_desc: [
		"Kaijin works from schematics for katana, long swords and spears. Craft a smithing bench (a smithing table, a crafting table, paper and planks) and set it up beside his anvil."
	]
	quest.3E112E381ADA60B4.title: "A Bench for the Smiths"
	quest.3E147C63E6EEBB67.quest_desc: [
		"Rigurd will not turn you out of Tempest, but he will not help you either: he points down the road. The Outcast Society is the pack's own faction (our interpretation), reincarnators and monsters that every nation rejected. Its contact waits where the road forks, out of the town's lamplight, and never gives a name."
		""
		"Go to the fork south of the gate and be seen to come alone."
	]
	quest.3E147C63E6EEBB67.quest_subtitle: "The dark road"
	quest.3E147C63E6EEBB67.title: "The Outcast's Mark"
	quest.3E7E77BB944CF7E0.quest_desc: [
		"Orcs eat everything and fear nothing, and they come in numbers. Cut ten of them down at the edge of their camp."
	]
	quest.3E7E77BB944CF7E0.title: "Pigs on Two Legs"
	quest.3F08093E46A35301.quest_desc: [
		"Cure a zombie villager: weakness, then a golden apple."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Faith for the advancement, and one more villager alive to trade with (Order)."
	]
	quest.3F08093E46A35301.title: "Zombie Doctor"
	quest.3F0BBF3FEC97C135.quest_desc: [
		"Breed 10 animals."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Order: tending animals adds a little Order karma."
	]
	quest.3F0BBF3FEC97C135.title: "Shepherd"
	quest.3F5B0360B52B7445.quest_desc: [
		"Rimuru learned his resistances by taking hits, not by studying. After the wolves have bitten you a few times, the world may start to answer: Physical Attack Resistance begins to form. Skills are never handed out by this book."
	]
	quest.3F5B0360B52B7445.title: "Thick Skin"
	quest.3FAB106A60C8B299.quest_desc: [
		"Kaijin was exiled from Dwargon and now leads production in Tempest, with Kurobe at the next anvil. They forge the first proper tools and katana. Bring 16 iron ingots and 16 coal to his open forge on the west road."
	]
	quest.3FAB106A60C8B299.title: "Tools for Kaijin"
	quest.40A33D79BFA6EAAC.quest_desc: [
		"Walk five kilometres on foot. Boats and horses do not count here: the Realm teaches itself through your soles."
		""
		"&7&o“The pedlars say a road you have walked is a road that will let you back.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor: new ground entered on foot counts (1 per 100 blocks, within a daily cap)."
	]
	quest.40A33D79BFA6EAAC.title: "A Long Walker"
	quest.4132F2C686AF15E9.quest_desc: [
		"Mine thirty-two cobbled deepslate. Below this line the stone turns grey and hard, and the diamonds start to show."
		""
		"&7&o“The deepslate has no name in the oldest songs. It is what the Realm is made of when it is not trying to be pretty.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Craft: diamonds mined down here count as much as shallow ones (2 each)."
	]
	quest.4132F2C686AF15E9.title: "Where the Stone Goes Dark"
	quest.41478DC3F02993DE.quest_desc: [
		"East of Tempest lies Lake Siss and its marsh, home of the lizardmen."
	]
	quest.41478DC3F02993DE.title: "Lake Siss"
	quest.41FB514E83118EA1.quest_desc: [
		"Find a pillager outpost. Scout it from a distance, clear it from the dark and take what the chest in the top holds."
		""
		"&7&o“No village sends envoys to an outpost. The envoys have simply stopped coming back.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor: pillagers are a new kind of foe (+4). Do not carry Bad Omen to a village: the raid that follows counts as a dark deed."
	]
	quest.41FB514E83118EA1.title: "A Tower in the Wilds"
	quest.41FBD44B4319CA87.quest_desc: [
		"North of the plaza the street climbs towards the royal terrace and the sound changes to hammers. This is where the kingdom's smiths live and work, house after house with a chimney."
	]
	quest.41FBD44B4319CA87.title: "The Forge Street"
	quest.4312441DAE604D7A.quest_desc: [
		"The limestone caves on the south shore are a labyrinth that is both fortress and seat of government. Chief Avalos holds court there; his men will fight from its tunnels. Find the entrance in the marsh."
	]
	quest.4312441DAE604D7A.title: "The Lizardmen's Caverns"
	quest.436E099F7CBD4215.quest_desc: [
		"Great Sage woke up in Rimuru's head before he knew what it was. Everyone in this world carries abilities, big or small, and the world notices when you first hold one. This quest is done when the world has registered any ability on you."
	]
	quest.436E099F7CBD4215.title: "Your First Ability"
	quest.43D60C8C4DC653A7.quest_desc: [
		"Gobta has told everyone he is the strongest goblin in the forest. He is also the one who, later on, beats the lizardman Gabiru in a duel (anime season 1, episode 11), so nobody laughs too hard. Today the boast is a horned rabbit, and he wants a witness."
		""
		"Kill five horned rabbits where he can hear about it."
	]
	quest.43D60C8C4DC653A7.quest_subtitle: "Strongest goblin in the forest"
	quest.43D60C8C4DC653A7.title: "Gobta's Great Boast"
	quest.43D7C9E691C19B2F.quest_desc: [
		"Win three raids that you did not bring: stand on the village's side when the horn sounds and be the last one standing."
		""
		"&7&o“A village that has been saved once is grateful. One that has been saved three times is simply used to you.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Order +30 per raid won (on a diminishing curve for repeats); Chaos +3 for each raid you brought on a village, so win only what is not your own."
	]
	quest.43D7C9E691C19B2F.title: "Shield of the Village"
	quest.443CA0DC588BEC52.quest_desc: [
		"Craft twelve sheets of paper and a Book and Quill. Write something down: your route, a date, or the name of someone who helped you."
		""
		"&7&o“The Realm has no printing press. It has patient people with ink and good eyes.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Faith: books feed enchanting, and every enchantment is +2."
	]
	quest.443CA0DC588BEC52.title: "The Scribe's Table"
	quest.4498A01D17D3F657.quest_desc: [
		"Rigurd leads the goblins and still lives in the old chief's hut in the goblins' quarter, north-east of the green. He served the tribe through the direwolf years and is the first to say what the town needs."
	]
	quest.4498A01D17D3F657.title: "Rigurd the Goblin Lord"
	quest.44C48A307109F375.quest_desc: [
		"Kaijin punched a minister, was tried in a court that never gave him a fair hearing, and was exiled with his brothers by the King's own word (anime season 1, episode 5). The smith does not say the King was wrong. He says it was the King's to say, and that a king can be asked again."
		""
		"Stand in his old forge and listen to what the hammer says about the man on the throne."
	]
	quest.44C48A307109F375.quest_subtitle: "What Kaijin remembers"
	quest.44C48A307109F375.title: "The Exile's Smithy"
	quest.44D8D55B843AB1D9.quest_desc: [
		"Rimuru wants houses raised on stone, not set in the mud. Mildo marks each plot and the goblins carry rock to it. Hand in 64 cobblestone."
	]
	quest.44D8D55B843AB1D9.title: "Stone Footings"
	quest.45F8FC6706DF4F4F.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a fishing rod and catch ten fish. A river is the only larder that fills itself while you sit."
		""
		"&7&o“A fisher and a farmer will argue the whole afternoon about which of them is more patient.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.45F8FC6706DF4F4F.title: "A Line in the Water"
	quest.464A5CC05EC762D9.quest_desc: [
		"Kaijin never has enough magic ore. Hand in two shards."
	]
	quest.464A5CC05EC762D9.quest_subtitle: "Gather"
	quest.464A5CC05EC762D9.title: "Shards for Kaijin"
	quest.46541EE000811D56.quest_desc: [
		"Craft shears and take six white wool from a sheep. A shorn sheep grows it back; a dead one does not."
		""
		"&7&o“The shepherds' rule is older than the village: take the wool, never the sheep.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.46541EE000811D56.title: "Shears and Wool"
	quest.46A849AD3B1F41C5.quest_desc: [
		"Find an ancient city. Slaying the Warden is the bravest, most foolish thing a mortal can do here; sneaking away is wise."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor +100 and a great foe, if you live. Most souls that try go to the Corridor early."
	]
	quest.46A849AD3B1F41C5.title: "The Deep Dark"
	quest.47AE71C4AA741918.quest_desc: [
		"Travel far: stand in a desert, a jungle, snowy plains and badlands. The Mortal Realm has large biomes; plan the trip."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor for distance (1 per 100 blocks from Wayfarer's Rest at your farthest) and Faith for the advancements on the way."
	]
	quest.47AE71C4AA741918.title: "The Wide World"
	quest.4895991B15F57CD2.quest_desc: [
		"A town that is not walked at dawn is a town that is not watched. Make your round of Tempest."
	]
	quest.4895991B15F57CD2.quest_subtitle: "Wander"
	quest.4895991B15F57CD2.title: "Round of the Town"
	quest.48B3E8CACE86A277.quest_desc: [
		"Dwarven smiths prize magic ore, iron soaked in magicules over centuries. Bring back a few shards."
	]
	quest.48B3E8CACE86A277.title: "Magic Ore"
	quest.4B1932600C991DF0.quest_desc: [
		"Mildo, the quiet dwarf who surveys and lays out the streets, needs timber for house frames and a lumber yard at the building site in the south-west. Hand in 32 oak logs."
	]
	quest.4B1932600C991DF0.title: "Timber for Mildo"
	quest.4B477A6841CB5326.quest_desc: [
		"Slay a pillager and a vindicator. Their outposts and mansions hide in the wild."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor: two more kinds of foe. Evokers and ravagers count as minor bosses (+10 each)."
	]
	quest.4B477A6841CB5326.title: "Illagers"
	quest.4B4B59B007A98EEC.quest_desc: [
		"A scribe's desk, a lectern, a banner of your own, a map of your own, a mason's saw and a shelf of reagents. You are a craftsman, whatever the Voice of the World will call you. The Ledger (chapter 0j) counts it as a way of life."
		""
		"&7&o“The old crafts did not die with the old kingdoms. They went on being useful, quietly, in a corner.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Craft and Faith are scored by the work itself (anvil, smithing, enchanting, brewing), not by this milestone."
	]
	quest.4B4B59B007A98EEC.quest_subtitle: "The crafts milestone"
	quest.4B4B59B007A98EEC.title: "Master of Hand and Cauldron"
	quest.4B97B9BA4541C6C9.quest_desc: [
		"The goblins, the direwolves, the kijin and the lizardmen fought the horde in the marsh together. Stand on the battlefield south-east of the lake and cut down twenty more orcs."
	]
	quest.4B97B9BA4541C6C9.title: "Hold the Line"
	quest.4BCFD8327B35499E.quest_desc: [
		"The Orc War is behind you and the council longhouse is quieter than it has been in months, which is the sort of quiet Souei does not like. Reports from the lake say the fish have gone and the water has begun to turn. Treyni's warning has come through the trees (our interpretation; in the anime a whirlpool calamity is sealed in the Beast Kingdom's borders and broken loose by Clayman's harlequins, episodes 17-18)."
		""
		"Stand on the green and hear what the scouts say before you choose your road."
	]
	quest.4BCFD8327B35499E.quest_subtitle: "Act IV begins"
	quest.4BCFD8327B35499E.title: "A Calamity Stirs"
	quest.4C0E3BFFAE3E50CA.quest_desc: [
		"Wild direwolves still prowl the forest edge. Drive off three."
	]
	quest.4C0E3BFFAE3E50CA.quest_subtitle: "Hunt"
	quest.4C0E3BFFAE3E50CA.title: "Wolves at the Edge"
	quest.4D73CAD0D78606DD.quest_desc: [
		"Clayman's agents Tear and Footman, the harlequins, are the ones who talk Phobio into carrying the seal and then watch it break (anime season 1, episodes 17-18). They want paying: not for the work, which they enjoy, but for being sure you are the kind of soul who pays."
		""
		"Meet them on the lake's western shore and hand in three silver coins."
	]
	quest.4D73CAD0D78606DD.quest_subtitle: "Clayman's errand-runners"
	quest.4D73CAD0D78606DD.title: "The Harlequins' Toll"
	quest.4D84DCDECB3CCFDC.quest_desc: [
		"Dwargon's word is only worth what is carried back to the people it was given for. The green in Tempest is where Rimuru's council meets, and the stew is better than the King's."
		""
		"Take the pact north and stand on the village green."
	]
	quest.4D84DCDECB3CCFDC.quest_subtitle: "Carry it home"
	quest.4D84DCDECB3CCFDC.title: "The King's Word"
	quest.4F752FC714E6D62C.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a stonecutter and use it five times. Stairs, slabs and walls of stone come out of it cleaner and cheaper than by hand."
		""
		"&7&o“The masons of the Realm do not carve; they release. The wall, they say, was always in the stone.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly: but infrastructure for others is Craft and Order in a village you help."
	]
	quest.4F752FC714E6D62C.title: "The Mason's Saw"
	quest.4FAAF7A1BC9ADF09.quest_desc: [
		"Punch a tree, make a crafting table, and trade your wooden tools for stone ones before night falls."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Small steps, but every advancement you earn in Life 1 adds Faith karma."
	]
	quest.4FAAF7A1BC9ADF09.title: "Wood and Stone"
	quest.4FE7A65646FF0ED9.quest_desc: [
		"Trade with villagers a hundred times. Level a villager to expert and you will see what they keep for the best customers."
		""
		"&7&o“A hundred trades and every librarian in the district knows how you take your tea.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Order: 1 per trade; the curve flattens, but a hundred trades is a name the Realm remembers."
	]
	quest.4FE7A65646FF0ED9.title: "Master Trader"
	quest.502D1D1020519DFF.quest_desc: [
		"The sick tent never has enough hipokute. Hand in six hipokute grass."
	]
	quest.502D1D1020519DFF.quest_subtitle: "Gather"
	quest.502D1D1020519DFF.title: "Herbs for the Infirmary"
	quest.50382544FBB449E8.quest_desc: [
		"You wake at Wayfarer's Rest, a human like any other. There is no respawn in this realm: the first death ends this life, and your soul moves on to the Spirit Corridor. Nothing you carry survives that crossing. What survives is what you did."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Every deed in this book feeds one of six karma axes: Valor, Order, Craft, Faith, Longevity, and the dark one, Chaos. Ask the Voice with /ttl guide."
	]
	quest.50382544FBB449E8.quest_subtitle: "Wayfarer's Rest"
	quest.50382544FBB449E8.title: "Only Once"
	quest.50CBFF631DD567A4.quest_desc: [
		"Follow the road north through the mountains to the gate of the Armed Nation of Dwargon, where King Gazel rules and the best smiths of the continent work."
	]
	quest.50CBFF631DD567A4.title: "The Dwarven Road"
	quest.50ED07BC02E5FED6.quest_desc: [
		"Build a furnace: eight cobblestone in a ring. Cook meat in it, smelt ore in it, and keep it burning."
		""
		"&7&o“A lit furnace is the only thing in a cold house that looks back at you kindly.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.50ED07BC02E5FED6.title: "A Fire in a Box"
	quest.51671CA0A5D6B5A4.quest_desc: [
		"A horde that kneels still has to eat. The Horde does not ask for bread: it asks for what the dead leave behind, and for someone who will not run when it is eaten (our interpretation of Starved, anime season 1, episode 12). Hand it over and it follows you."
		""
		"Stand in the camp and hand in thirty-two pieces of rotten flesh."
	]
	quest.51671CA0A5D6B5A4.quest_subtitle: "Feed the hunger"
	quest.51671CA0A5D6B5A4.title: "The Horde Kneels"
	quest.519D3CA856E8F7CB.quest_desc: [
		"Stay alive for 2 days (about 40 minutes of play)."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Longevity: 2 days is the least a soul needs to be judged a Survivor."
	]
	quest.519D3CA856E8F7CB.title: "Two Days"
	quest.51A3E20507BA0C02.quest_desc: [
		"Make a crafting table. Place it where you will come back to it: this is the first corner of whatever you build."
		""
		"&7&o“The innkeeper at Wayfarer's Rest says a man is worth what he can make on a bench.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly: it is the first step of every craft that is."
	]
	quest.51A3E20507BA0C02.title: "A Table to Work At"
	quest.51BB29F904813A27.quest_desc: [
		"Gazel is not an opponent for the unprepared: in Tensura's own fight he has the full strength of the Hero King, and he draws more of it when he is hurt. Reach 10,000 EP and carry a plan, whether it is steel, fire or a party."
	]
	quest.51BB29F904813A27.quest_subtitle: "10,000 EP"
	quest.51BB29F904813A27.title: "A King's Equal"
	quest.51BE6D1FFA78B4AF.quest_desc: [
		"Nine ways of life are open to a mortal here: the traveller, the householder, the farmer, the miner, the explorer, the villager, the craftsman, the Nether-walker and the one who stood before the End. The Voice has written down every one you finished. Five is enough: nobody does it all, and nobody is asked to."
		""
		"&7&o“In a ledger, the zero entries are the ones that tell you most about a person.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Nothing is scored here: this only counts the milestones above."
	]
	quest.51BE6D1FFA78B4AF.quest_subtitle: "Five ways of life"
	quest.51BE6D1FFA78B4AF.title: "The Ledger"
	quest.51FF35F087F1E23D.quest_desc: [
		"Milim arrived at Tempest like a storm and stayed for the honey: Rimuru calmed the Dragonoid Demon Lord with something sweet and she called him a friend (anime season 1, episode 16). A friend of Tempest is worth a few jars. Take eight bottles of honey to Milim's domain, in the lands to the far south-east (about 2,500 blocks from Tempest), and ask what she thinks of the lake."
		""
		"Hand in eight honey bottles in the City of the Forgotten Dragon, where Milim keeps her court."
	]
	quest.51FF35F087F1E23D.quest_subtitle: "The light road"
	quest.51FF35F087F1E23D.title: "Honey for a Demon Lord"
	quest.520F289E26CD8D14.quest_desc: [
		"The Hero King is a hard man to beat and a good one to lose to. When he falls, he bows his head, and the court will tell it as a duel and nothing else. No reputation is lost with Dwargon because of it."
	]
	quest.520F289E26CD8D14.quest_subtitle: "Defeat Gazel Dwargo"
	quest.520F289E26CD8D14.title: "The Honour Duel"
	quest.522F16F19507224C.quest_desc: [
		"You have a table, a fire, light, a chest and a blade. That is more than most mortals own, and more than enough to leave the doorstep. Tick this off when you are ready to build a home, plant a field or go down a shaft."
		""
		"&7&o“At Wayfarer's Rest they ring the bell once for a traveller who has packed well.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Longevity first: nothing else you do in this book matters if you do not live to do it."
	]
	quest.522F16F19507224C.quest_subtitle: "The first milestone"
	quest.522F16F19507224C.title: "Ready for the Road"
	quest.52EC32EBD77A5F6A.quest_desc: [
		"Tame an animal: a wolf with bones, a cat with fish, a horse with patience. The Realm is lonely at night."
		""
		"&7&o“The hounds of Wayfarer's Rest follow nobody. They choose, and when they have chosen, it is for life, which in the Realm is a promise.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Faith for the advancement (+2). Animals you tame are a sort of Order: you are now responsible for them."
	]
	quest.52EC32EBD77A5F6A.title: "A Loyal Friend"
	quest.531A7A2DD9F75DC8.quest_desc: [
		"In the story Milim hits Charybdis when Rimuru asks (anime season 1, episode 19). In Tempest's world she is on the far side of the map, and the lake is still yours to hold. Anyone may fight Charybdis, whatever road they walk."
		""
		"Stand on the shore and claim the reward to bring it up. It rises over the water, summons nothing but waves, and turns furious at 60% and again at 30% of its health. Bring a party, and stay out of the water."
		""
		"&6If the call fails&r (Charybdis is already out, or still resting from the last fight: 72 hours), type /ttl story fight charybdis on the shore, within 96 blocks of the arena's centre (635, 145)."
	]
	quest.531A7A2DD9F75DC8.quest_subtitle: "Begin the fight"
	quest.531A7A2DD9F75DC8.title: "Face the Whirlpool"
	quest.5324FB850E375029.quest_desc: [
		"Breed thirty animals. A herd you keep is food for a village and a reason for other people to stay."
		""
		"&7&o“A shepherd's wealth is counted in the lambs of the lambs.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Order: 0.5 per animal bred, on the diminishing log curve, so the first few score most."
	]
	quest.5324FB850E375029.title: "Keeper of Herds"
	quest.53C77B16D89F8A29.quest_desc: [
		"Ready? Gazel will not strike a soul that has not asked. Claim the reward at the throne to start the duel, or use \"Challenge the King\" in his dialog. He draws his full strength at half health, so keep your party close and your healing within reach."
		""
		"&6If the call fails&r (the King is already out, or still resting from the last fight: 72 hours), type /ttl story fight gazel_dwargo at the throne."
	]
	quest.53C77B16D89F8A29.quest_subtitle: "Begin the duel"
	quest.53C77B16D89F8A29.title: "Challenge the King"
	quest.548B40BA65FF6779.quest_desc: [
		"Smelt sand into glass and cut it into eight panes. Windows keep the weather out and let you watch the road."
		""
		"&7&o“Glass is the Realm's quiet luxury: the dwarves would call it sand with ambition.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.548B40BA65FF6779.title: "Let in the Light"
	quest.5510D365D50CF905.quest_desc: [
		"You have been below the sea level and back. A line of rails behind you, a geode in the pack, obsidian in the chest, deepslate under your boots. Tick it off when you have what you came for; The Ledger (chapter 0j) counts it as a way of life."
		""
		"&7&o“The miners' guild at Wayfarer's Rest has one rule: the last one out turns off no light.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Craft: every diamond and every ancient debris you mined is already scored; this milestone only says you did it."
	]
	quest.5510D365D50CF905.quest_subtitle: "The mining milestone"
	quest.5510D365D50CF905.title: "Deep Delver"
	quest.5519CECDD67BEDC0.quest_desc: [
		"Find a bastion remnant: a ruined piglin fortress of blackstone, with chests of gold and a strong guard of piglin brutes. Go in quietly, in gold."
		""
		"&7&o“Whoever built the bastions fled in a hurry. The piglins who remained have been guarding the leftovers ever since.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor for the walking, and the brutes are a hard kind of foe."
	]
	quest.5519CECDD67BEDC0.title: "A Bastion in the Dark"
	quest.5532E5E94F18A457.quest_desc: [
		"Collect dragon's breath in a glass bottle from a lingering cloud left by the dragon. A bottle of it makes lingering potions."
		""
		"&7&o“A dragon's breath is the one thing in the Realm that smells of nothing, and has the longest memory.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Faith for the advancement (+2)."
	]
	quest.5532E5E94F18A457.title: "You Need a Mint"
	quest.5557926F5E401552.quest_desc: [
		"You killed the Mortal Dragon, lived thirty days, finished five ways of life and walked back to the bell. When this life ends, and it will, the Voice of the World will read what the world remembers: the great foe, the days, the deeds. This is the shape of a Legend. It is yours whether the Voice calls it so or not."
		""
		"&7&o“They will say it began at a crossroads with a bell and ended somewhere else, and that is the whole of the truth.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Legend tier: a great foe, at least 30 days and enough karma, scored by the karma engine at death, not by this book."
	]
	quest.5557926F5E401552.quest_subtitle: "The finale of the first life"
	quest.5557926F5E401552.title: "A Life That Counted"
	quest.556EA88DAE9171BE.quest_desc: [
		"Shion's stew needs meat, and horned rabbits are everywhere. Bring down six."
	]
	quest.556EA88DAE9171BE.quest_subtitle: "Hunt"
	quest.556EA88DAE9171BE.title: "Horned Rabbit Stew"
	quest.56EB250D2EBACC74.quest_desc: [
		"The dwarf trainers sell battlewill manuals that teach their own arts. Buy and read one, then practise until the technique is yours: Aura Sword, Instant Move or Violent Break. This quest checks for Aura Sword."
	]
	quest.56EB250D2EBACC74.title: "A Dwarven Battlewill Manual"
	quest.571629DA10EF5830.quest_desc: [
		"The goblins who fought the direwolves now ride them: after the naming the pack became the Tempest Wolves and the goblins became their riders (anime season 1, episode 3). A town that holds the forest needs someone who can talk to the wolves."
		""
		"Win a direwolf over (tame one) and show Tempest the road is not only a fight."
	]
	quest.571629DA10EF5830.quest_subtitle: "The riders of Tempest"
	quest.571629DA10EF5830.title: "Hear Me, Direwolves"
	quest.57DB2952F54CA2BE.quest_desc: [
		"Stay alive for 15 days (5 hours of play)."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Longevity: the longer you live, the more the axis gives, but less with every day (the curve flattens)."
	]
	quest.57DB2952F54CA2BE.title: "Half a Moon"
	quest.57F95C93A1BA166D.quest_desc: [
		"Hand in sixteen loaves of bread, to be shared with the village's hungry. Nobody will check who the loaves go to; you will know."
		""
		"&7&o“A village that has had a bad winter does not say so. It only goes quiet near the bakery.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored: the book cannot see a gift, and the Voice scores only what the world records. Do it anyway."
	]
	quest.57F95C93A1BA166D.title: "Bread for the Hungry"
	quest.589B9EDB1263A248.quest_desc: [
		"A king that ate the strongest of his own to become a calamity (anime season 1, episodes 12-13). When he falls, the horde does not fall with him: it is still starving, and it has still no leader."
	]
	quest.589B9EDB1263A248.quest_subtitle: "Defeat the Orc Lord"
	quest.589B9EDB1263A248.title: "Geld Falls"
	quest.58AA1E63ACF93062.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a golden helmet and distract a piglin by dropping a gold ingot in front of it. Piglins ignore anyone in gold armour; a bartering piglin is a sure source of ender pearls."
		""
		"&7&o“The piglins do not ask what you want. They only ask what you are carrying.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Faith for the advancement (+2)."
	]
	quest.58AA1E63ACF93062.title: "Oh, Shiny"
	quest.595C87BDF9A55477.quest_desc: [
		"Craft three books, set one on a lectern and open it. Villagers will hold a lectern job for it, and a quiet corner is all a reader needs."
		""
		"&7&o“A lectern stands in front of the best light in the house; the Realm's scholars arrange their lives around that.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly: lecterns are what a librarian looks for, and librarians sell enchanted books (trades: Order)."
	]
	quest.595C87BDF9A55477.title: "A Reader at the Lectern"
	quest.59608580FB3801D4.quest_desc: [
		"Before Rimuru named them, the ogres had a hidden village in the north-east hills. The orcs burned it and killed most of its people; the six survivors came to Tempest. A burned tower marks the site. This position is our own estimate from the fan map, so look around the hills if you do not find it at once."
	]
	quest.59608580FB3801D4.title: "Ashes of the Kijin Village"
	quest.59A17C1D26897630.quest_desc: [
		"Cross a soul sand valley and bring back sixteen blocks of soul sand. It slows your feet and whispers; the skeletons here are the worst."
		""
		"&7&o“The valley's sand is said to hold the last breath of everyone who ever lost a fight here. It does not bother to say which fight.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor for the walking."
	]
	quest.59A17C1D26897630.title: "The Valley of Souls"
	quest.59F4870034DD1420.quest_desc: [
		"In the anime the harlequins persuade Phobio to let Charybdis possess him, and the seal breaks (anime season 1, episode 18). Here the seal breaks because you broke it: Charybdis is Clayman's weapon, and the dark road holds the knife. Anyone may fight Charybdis, whatever road they walk."
		""
		"Stand on the shore and claim the reward to bring it up. It rises over the water and turns furious at 60% and again at 30% of its health. The claim also records the story flag \"charybdis_woke\"."
		""
		"&6If the call fails&r (Charybdis is already out, or still resting from the last fight: 72 hours), type /ttl story fight charybdis on the shore, within 96 blocks of the arena's centre (635, 145)."
	]
	quest.59F4870034DD1420.quest_subtitle: "Begin the fight"
	quest.59F4870034DD1420.title: "Wake the Calamity"
	quest.5A428C02809011D3.quest_desc: [
		"Slay the Nether's own: a blaze, a ghast, a wither skeleton and a magma cube."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor: four kinds of foe, 4 Valor karma each."
	]
	quest.5A428C02809011D3.title: "Fire and Bone"
	quest.5AC90B7245A5B5DC.quest_desc: [
		"Halfway up the road, inside the dwarves' border, stands a village of stone and spruce with copper roofs: smithy, library and market in one. It is the first sign that you have left the forest behind."
	]
	quest.5AC90B7245A5B5DC.title: "A Dwarven Waystation"
	quest.5BE93F04F60FB5AA.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a wooden pickaxe, a wooden axe and a wooden sword. Soft tools, but they are enough to reach stone."
		""
		"&7&o“Poor tools break first, and teach the hands what the good ones will need.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly. Wood leads to stone, and stone to iron and Craft karma."
	]
	quest.5BE93F04F60FB5AA.title: "Wooden Tools"
	quest.5C3910E005FDD1EA.quest_desc: [
		"Build an enchanting table and enchant something."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Faith: every enchantment adds Faith karma. Faith souls lean towards Elves, spirits and sage-type skills."
	]
	quest.5C3910E005FDD1EA.title: "Words of Power"
	quest.5C6CEA9703648161.quest_desc: [
		"Any three of the deeds are enough. Feed, light, arm, warm, defend, keep a herd, raise an iron guardian or save a village: a village needs all of these and rarely gets even one. Tick it off when you would not mind them telling the story."
		""
		"&7&o“A name in the Realm is not what you are called. It is what people say when you leave the room.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Order and Valor are scored by what the world records; this milestone only says you did the rest."
	]
	quest.5C6CEA9703648161.quest_subtitle: "The deeds milestone"
	quest.5C6CEA9703648161.title: "A Good Name"
	quest.5CCC0C26065B405A.quest_desc: [
		"Stand on the marsh battlefield where two hundred thousand orcs met the forest alliance."
	]
	quest.5CCC0C26065B405A.title: "Where the Orc Lord Fell"
	quest.5CE177F176862D46.quest_desc: [
		"Dwargon keeps its word with those who stand with the free peoples. A soul that comes with an open hand gets an open offer: an honour duel, King against petitioner, with nothing held against the one who wins. Tensura's own throne room greets a hero the same way, with a training fight."
		""
		"Stand before the throne and accept the terms. The King's word is set down for you at once: your duel costs Dwargon's goodwill nothing, and the word is spent when the duel is fought."
	]
	quest.5CE177F176862D46.quest_subtitle: "The light road"
	quest.5CE177F176862D46.title: "Terms of Honour"
	quest.5D7D7960B5EA0119.quest_desc: [
		"Find a nether fossil buried in the soul sand valley: a ribcage as large as a house. Bone blocks, and nobody to ask whose they were."
		""
		"&7&o“The Nether has no history that anyone has ever written down. The fossil is simply proof that it once had a past.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor for the walking."
	]
	quest.5D7D7960B5EA0119.title: "The Bones of Something Large"
	quest.5DC6BB895E05778A.quest_desc: [
		"A horde with no king eats itself, and a king that eats too much becomes something worse: the Orc Disaster, the catastrophe the Horde called its champion until it turned on the one who had taken its throne (anime season 1, episode 14: Geld devours Gelmud and the dead around him and rises again)."
		""
		"Stand on the battlefield and claim the reward to start the fight. More health than the Lord, a starving horde behind it, and a frenzy at 30% health."
		""
		"&6If the call fails&r (the Disaster is already out, or resting: 48 hours), type /ttl story fight orc_disaster at the battlefield."
	]
	quest.5DC6BB895E05778A.quest_subtitle: "Begin the last battle"
	quest.5DC6BB895E05778A.title: "The Champion Turns"
	quest.5DD9D39B70567F80.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a barrel and four chests. Sort them: food, stone, ore, tools. A house that cannot find its own things is only a heap."
		""
		"&7&o“A tidy storeroom is the only wealth a poor household can show off.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.5DD9D39B70567F80.title: "A Proper Storeroom"
	quest.5DDBDC9CF595C24E.quest_desc: [
		"Gabiru lost a duel to Gobta, took his father's seat when the old chieftain would not wait, and led the lizardmen into the orcs alone (anime season 1, episodes 11-12). His warriors are the ones bleeding at the lake. The pride is his; the wounds belong to everyone."
		""
		"Go to the caverns and hand in four low potions for the wounded."
	]
	quest.5DDBDC9CF595C24E.quest_subtitle: "The light road"
	quest.5DDBDC9CF595C24E.title: "Gabiru's Pride"
	quest.5E6EA0308CD76328.quest_desc: [
		"Walk back to Wayfarer's Rest and stand at the bell where you began. See who is still there, and who has come in since."
		""
		"&7&o“The innkeeper does not say welcome back. She sets a place at the table, which is the same thing and keeps better.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Longevity: you stayed alive to come back."
	]
	quest.5E6EA0308CD76328.title: "Come Home"
	quest.5F1A8DCF7C0E73A4.quest_desc: [
		"Build a Nether portal and step through. It leads to the Mortal Nether, which belongs to this life only. Bring fire resistance if you can, and never dig straight down."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor: walking the Mortal Nether adds 20 Valor karma, once."
	]
	quest.5F1A8DCF7C0E73A4.title: "The Mortal Nether"
	quest.5F297D5C1B0D00D8.quest_desc: [
		"Trade with villagers 25 times."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Order: 1 karma per trade. The log curve means the first trades count the most."
	]
	quest.5F297D5C1B0D00D8.title: "A Known Face"
	quest.5F709D2F4385C2DB.quest_desc: [
		"Hold sixteen baked potatoes, eight cooked beef and eight cooked porkchops. This is a week's food, and a week is a long time in a first life."
		""
		"&7&o“An empty larder in February is how most villages in the Realm lost their youngest saint.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Longevity: food buys days."
	]
	quest.5F709D2F4385C2DB.title: "A Full Larder"
	quest.60226F8162DAD560.quest_desc: [
		"Slay shulkers for two shulker shells, then craft a shulker box. It holds a stack of everything and keeps it when you drop it."
		""
		"&7&o“Shulkers have the patience of stones and the manners of knives.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor: shulkers are a new kind of foe (+4)."
	]
	quest.60226F8162DAD560.title: "A Box That Bites"
	quest.60A6E30719D91FFE.quest_desc: [
		"Stay alive for 7 days (about 2 hours and 20 minutes of play)."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Longevity: 7 days is the least a soul needs to be judged a Hero."
	]
	quest.60A6E30719D91FFE.title: "A Week"
	quest.60EF9E8FB35BF30E.quest_desc: [
		"Hand in eight white wool for the villagers who spent the winter in a draught. A blanket is the cheapest kindness there is."
		""
		"&7&o“The tailor of Wayfarer's Rest sews a name into each blanket, to see which one comes back and which stays.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored."
	]
	quest.60EF9E8FB35BF30E.title: "Wool for the Cold"
	quest.60F244EA243A900D.quest_desc: [
		"Geld, the Orc Lord, ate the strongest of his own army to become a monster that no one in the forest could face alone. He lies at the heart of the horde. This quest needs a real orc lord to be alive in the camp when you get there; the landmark spawns one, but another player may have killed it first. Come prepared, and do not come alone."
	]
	quest.60F244EA243A900D.quest_subtitle: "Geld, king of the hungry"
	quest.60F244EA243A900D.title: "The Orc Lord"
	quest.6159774165FC77C9.quest_desc: [
		"A round plaza with a fountain, twelve market stalls under white awnings, and every nation's merchants shouting prices. Dwargon stays neutral so that everyone trades here."
	]
	quest.6159774165FC77C9.title: "The Market Plaza"
	quest.615D609A3A9097CA.quest_desc: [
		"Dwarves also trade magic tomes of the basic elemental spells. Buy one and learn Wind Cutter, the first blade the smiths' apprentices pick up."
	]
	quest.615D609A3A9097CA.title: "A Dwarven Magic Tome"
	quest.619B66622F524091.quest_desc: [
		"The Outcast Society buys what Dwargon will not sell (our interpretation). Kaijin does not say who asked; he only says the Outcasts pay well for plans of the Dwargon forges, and that he did not say it. A third voice in the plaza says more: the King can be taken the hard way, or the quiet one."
		""
		"Stand among the stalls of the market plaza and let the broker find you."
	]
	quest.619B66622F524091.quest_subtitle: "The dark road"
	quest.619B66622F524091.title: "A Whisper in the Plaza"
	quest.623600D6FAEBFE01.quest_desc: [
		"Silver is the dwarves' favourite plain metal: it holds an enchantment and is the base of mithril. Find silver ore or buy it, and smelt an ingot."
	]
	quest.623600D6FAEBFE01.title: "Silver for the Smiths"
	quest.62BAB9C92E92D502.quest_desc: [
		"Visit a desert, a savanna, a snowy and a taiga village. Each builds in what its land gives: sandstone, acacia, snow, spruce."
		""
		"&7&o“You can tell where a stranger is from by how they build, and what they put over the door.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor for the ground covered; Order for each village you trade in."
	]
	quest.62BAB9C92E92D502.title: "Four Kinds of Hearth"
	quest.62FE2D23A04A949E.quest_desc: [
		"Hang two item frames and a painting. Put the best thing you own where the guests will see it."
		""
		"&7&o“A bare wall is a promise. A hung painting is the first sign somebody means to stay.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.62FE2D23A04A949E.title: "Make It Yours"
	quest.6386322E39091298.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a Sophisticated Storage chest. It holds the same things as a plain one and lets you label and keep them in order."
		""
		"&7&o“Itinerant joiners sell these from the back of a cart: dearer than a plain chest, and worth every nail.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.6386322E39091298.title: "A Better Chest"
	quest.6393057B0136AB75.quest_desc: [
		"Work a smithing table 5 times: netherite upgrades, armour trims."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Craft: every use of a smithing table adds 2 Craft karma."
	]
	quest.6393057B0136AB75.title: "The Smith's Art"
	quest.63A48763F37F8D6C.quest_desc: [
		"Rimuru moved the village to open ground with room to grow and water close by, and insisted on proper houses and roads from the first day. Stand on the green by the cooking fire: every plan in Tempest starts here."
	]
	quest.63A48763F37F8D6C.quest_subtitle: "The village green"
	quest.63A48763F37F8D6C.title: "A Town on Open Ground"
	quest.63A6DD3BF5669ACE.quest_desc: [
		"Find the caverns of the lizardmen south of the lake, where Chief Avalos ruled and his son Gabiru dreamed of glory."
	]
	quest.63A6DD3BF5669ACE.title: "The Lizardmen's Caverns"
	quest.64018361CB47A52B.quest_desc: [
		"Hand in thirty-two arrows for whoever keeps the road: the guards, the hunters, an old woman with a bow."
		""
		"&7&o“She has not missed since the war, and the war was before anyone's grandmother.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored."
	]
	quest.64018361CB47A52B.title: "Arrows for the Guard"
	quest.64380F006D6AFF5B.quest_desc: [
		"Find a woodland mansion deep in a dark forest. It is the deadliest building in the Realm and holds a Totem of Undying for those who return."
		""
		"&7&o“Nobody remembers who lived there. The ones who have gone in say the rooms are still being kept tidy.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor for the distance, and minor bosses: evokers and vindicators are foes (+4 / +10)."
	]
	quest.64380F006D6AFF5B.title: "The Woodland Mansion"
	quest.644083476DBFE88A.quest_desc: [
		"Bring back a ghast tear and four magma cream: regeneration and fire resistance. You will want the second before anything else down here."
		""
		"&7&o“A ghast weeps for nobody in particular. A brewer collects what falls.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Faith for the brewing it feeds (0.5 per use)."
	]
	quest.644083476DBFE88A.title: "Tears and Cream"
	quest.64E84EC2992F8D82.quest_desc: [
		"Walls, furnaces and footings: all of them want cobblestone. Hand in 32."
	]
	quest.64E84EC2992F8D82.quest_subtitle: "Gather"
	quest.64E84EC2992F8D82.title: "A Day's Stone"
	quest.654329C1B385D470.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a cartography table and a filled map of your surroundings. Extend it as you walk; a map the size of a day's journey costs a little paper."
		""
		"&7&o“The cartographer at the crossroads has never left it. He knows every road by how many sheets it took.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly: a map helps Valor's distance, and the compass at chapter 0e's end ends the guessing."
	]
	quest.654329C1B385D470.title: "The Cartographer's Desk"
	quest.654B3760F245A721.quest_desc: [
		"Every house, door and fence starts as a tree. Hand in 16 oak logs."
	]
	quest.654B3760F245A721.quest_subtitle: "Gather"
	quest.654B3760F245A721.title: "A Day's Wood"
	quest.65B824C8927B1E9A.quest_desc: [
		"Hold a bow and sixty-four arrows. Crystals on the tall towers can only be reached by arrow."
		""
		"&7&o“A dragon is a long way to throw a stone at. That is why we make arrows.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly: kills with them are Valor."
	]
	quest.65B824C8927B1E9A.title: "Sixty-Four Arrows"
	quest.661F65069D6D27BB.quest_desc: [
		"Find a swamp hut and an igloo. One belongs to a witch, one to nobody. The igloo's cellar has a stair behind the bed."
		""
		"&7&o“A swamp witch only asks that you wipe your boots. It is the people who do not who find out why.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor for the ground covered; kills of a witch count as a new kind of foe (+4 Valor)."
	]
	quest.661F65069D6D27BB.title: "Witches and Igloos"
	quest.66CC4813FDE91493.quest_desc: [
		"Bread in the oven, eggs in the basket, a full larder, a dog at the door and fish on the line. No one who owns this list has gone hungry in a long time. It is one of the ways of life that The Ledger (chapter 0j) adds up."
		""
		"&7&o“They hold the harvest feast when the last sheaf is in. Whoever brought the first seed is, by old custom, served first.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Longevity: you will not starve."
	]
	quest.66CC4813FDE91493.quest_subtitle: "The farming milestone"
	quest.66CC4813FDE91493.title: "Harvest Home"
	quest.6786C757A8E0F60A.quest_desc: [
		"Kaijin's trade secret: iron and magic ore melted together in a kiln make magisteel, a metal that carries magicules. A kiln is expensive (blast furnace, cauldron, obsidian and a netherite ingot), so this one is for the dedicated."
	]
	quest.6786C757A8E0F60A.title: "Feeling Low?"
	quest.67B8853DC7F4D8B5.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a chest and put your spare stone and wood in it. A full pack is how you end up dying with your hands holding the wrong thing."
		""
		"&7&o“Wayfarer's Rest has a hundred chests behind its doors and not one with a lock; the Realm trusts the road.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.67B8853DC7F4D8B5.title: "A Place for Things"
	quest.68F504149DB6ABF0.quest_desc: [
		"The Outcast contact has a letter for you and no name for whoever wrote it (our interpretation: the hand is Yuuki Kagurazaka's, the Free Guild's Grandmaster, who appears in anime season 1, episode 20, and Clayman is the one who profits). The letter says that a Demon Lord with a fondness for puppets is gathering a beast prince's grief and a sealed calamity in one place, and that someone has to be standing at the lake when it comes up."
		""
		"Go to the fork south of Tempest's gate."
	]
	quest.68F504149DB6ABF0.quest_subtitle: "The dark road"
	quest.68F504149DB6ABF0.title: "The Unsigned Letter"
	quest.69634DC941547E1C.quest_desc: [
		"Behind the gate a long tunnel climbs into the mountain, then opens on a cavern city: lit windows, shop signs, lamps strung across the street and bridges high above. Walk the south street."
	]
	quest.69634DC941547E1C.title: "Through the Tunnel"
	quest.6A02570FD1A84087.quest_desc: [
		"Dwargon will not forgive a dead king, and the guards will not look the other way after. Kill the Hero King and the kingdom turns on you."
		""
		"&6Why it matters:&r no honour: the kill costs Dwargon -60 (Hostile, guards attack) and sets the flag \"regicide\", which opens the Corruption twist for a light soul too."
	]
	quest.6A02570FD1A84087.quest_subtitle: "Defeat Gazel Dwargo"
	quest.6A02570FD1A84087.title: "Regicide"
	quest.6A14E30FE7F5E819.quest_desc: [
		"In the story the Orc Lord devoured the majin Gelmud, the schemer who had named him, and evolved into the Orc Disaster, a calamity-class monster. An epilogue for the very strong: defeat an Orc Disaster."
	]
	quest.6A14E30FE7F5E819.title: "Eat or Be Eaten"
	quest.6AA6AC10181F3F11.quest_desc: [
		"Build an iron golem to guard a village."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Order and Faith: an advancement, and a village that can defend itself. Killing a golem is a Chaos deed."
	]
	quest.6AA6AC10181F3F11.title: "Hired Help"
	quest.6BFA5D9C19308004.quest_desc: [
		"At the back of the cavern, behind the great stair and the royal terrace, sits the third king of Dwargon in his throne room of tuff and deepslate, under red banners. He has ruled for over three hundred years and judges every petitioner himself. He sits there as a silent guardian (he does not speak and does not fight): kneel, then leave."
	]
	quest.6BFA5D9C19308004.quest_subtitle: "Gazel Dwargo, the Hero King"
	quest.6BFA5D9C19308004.title: "An Audience with King Gazel"
	quest.6BFF3AB595F9426A.quest_desc: [
		"Reach 50,000 EP. At this strength a single fighter can turn a skirmish, as the kijin did on the battlefield."
	]
	quest.6BFF3AB595F9426A.title: "A Walking Calamity"
	quest.6C4DDD673A2A254A.quest_desc: [
		"Collect blaze rods: you need them for brewing stands and Eyes of Ender."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor for the blazes you slay; Faith later, when you brew with them."
	]
	quest.6C4DDD673A2A254A.title: "Blaze Rods"
	quest.6CF85FBDB2D29F4C.quest_desc: [
		"East of the plaza the engineers keep their workshop, a hall of casings, shafts and turning cogs. Dwargon is the first place on this continent that runs machines. Look inside."
	]
	quest.6CF85FBDB2D29F4C.title: "The Engineers' Workshop"
	quest.6DAB90333F617B16.quest_desc: [
		"Gather hipokute grass, the magicule-rich herb the slime turned into full potions. Healing in this world starts here."
	]
	quest.6DAB90333F617B16.title: "Hipokute Herbs"
	quest.6DDF459E16D36563.quest_desc: [
		"Act II ends with the King measured, one way or the other. Dwargon will remember what was done in its throne room, and so will everyone who trades with it. Claim the reward to close the act: it records Act II and applies its reputation (light: Dwargon +15; dark: Dwargon -20, Outcast Society +10)."
	]
	quest.6DDF459E16D36563.quest_subtitle: "Act II"
	quest.6DDF459E16D36563.title: "The Armed Nation"
	quest.6E5B3A4C9692E518.quest_desc: [
		"Skeletons shoot from the dark and never miss twice. Shut up eight of them."
	]
	quest.6E5B3A4C9692E518.quest_subtitle: "Hunt"
	quest.6E5B3A4C9692E518.title: "Quiet the Bowmen"
	quest.6EC64E409D27BB66.quest_desc: [
		"Slay five pillagers who would raid a village's roads. Fight them where the farms are, not where the folk are."
		""
		"&7&o“Raiders count on a village not being able to say no. It is a kindness to say it for them.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor: pillagers are a kind of foe (+4 for the first, little after). A raid you did not start and won is Order (+30)."
	]
	quest.6EC64E409D27BB66.title: "Keep the Peace"
	quest.6ED182178A90CB23.quest_desc: [
		"The Horde's envoy you met in the empty goblin huts was only the first word. Geld's army has a masked patron, Gelmud, who feeds the king's hunger with promises (anime season 1, episode 10), and an army that size needs strong blades more than it needs loyalty (our interpretation: the Outcast Society passes yours along)."
		""
		"Walk into the orc camp and be seen. Orcs do not make distinctions between hungry and hunted, so keep your sword out."
	]
	quest.6ED182178A90CB23.quest_subtitle: "The dark road"
	quest.6ED182178A90CB23.title: "The Horde's Welcome"
	quest.6EFF5511B028B9AC.quest_desc: [
		"Find or buy a smithing schematic and use it. Kaijin's craft starts with a single page."
	]
	quest.6EFF5511B028B9AC.title: "Start Smithing"
	quest.6F54281B6FBEDD14.quest_desc: [
		"Find the stronghold and its portal room."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Exploring far from Wayfarer's Rest adds Valor karma (1 per 100 blocks of your farthest trip)."
	]
	quest.6F54281B6FBEDD14.title: "The Stronghold"
	quest.7070BCCFF604CC3C.quest_desc: [
		"North-west of Tempest lies the cave where the Storm Dragon Veldora was sealed for three hundred years, and where a slime woke up with a Great Sage in his head."
	]
	quest.7070BCCFF604CC3C.title: "The Sealed Cave"
	quest.7084AFF4A1F3AAC4.quest_desc: [
		"Your strength in this world is measured in EP (existence points): magicules plus aura. Defeating monsters makes you stronger. Reach 5,000 EP, where common skills start to answer."
	]
	quest.7084AFF4A1F3AAC4.title: "Existence Points"
	quest.7088AFEA47B54D28.quest_desc: [
		"Make a bow and sixteen arrows. String comes from spiders and flint from gravel; a bow keeps a creeper at a respectful distance."
		""
		"&7&o“A sword is for the quarrel you chose. A bow is for the one that chose you.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly: kills are Valor, and the first kind of every foe counts the most."
	]
	quest.7088AFEA47B54D28.title: "Something to Hold the Night Off"
	quest.70EB5B4005F7C8E2.quest_desc: [
		"Mine thirty-two netherrack and lay a short road away from your portal. Never walk blind: the floor here ends in lava as often as in rock."
		""
		"&7&o“The first road in the Nether was laid by someone who did not come back. The second by someone who followed their footprints.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor: the Mortal Nether adds +20 once for walking in it."
	]
	quest.70EB5B4005F7C8E2.title: "The Netherrack Road"
	quest.7120FAE119C8B75E.quest_desc: [
		"Shuna leads the goblin women at the looms and clothes the whole town, down to the riders. She has more weavers than thread. Hand in 16 string and 16 white wool and visit her weaving hut on the east road."
	]
	quest.7120FAE119C8B75E.title: "Cloth for Shuna"
	quest.7135883F76B91D2C.quest_desc: [
		"Dig up buried treasure. A map from a shipwreck or ruin shows the spot; the chest holds a Heart of the Sea."
		""
		"&7&o“They always bury it above the tide line. They always forget the tide moves.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor and a little Faith: it is a journey and a find."
	]
	quest.7135883F76B91D2C.title: "X Marks the Sand"
	quest.71484AC8A112CDDE.quest_desc: [
		"In the story the hunger does not die with Geld; the Orc Lord's Starved skill drives the horde on (anime season 1, episodes 12 and 14). Here it passes to whoever stands over him. The claim records that you lead the Horde now: the story flag \"horde_leader\" is set, a mark only the dark road can earn."
		""
		"&6Why it matters:&r the Horde's goodwill (Orc Horde +40) is paid when Act III closes."
	]
	quest.71484AC8A112CDDE.quest_subtitle: "Defeat the Orc Lord"
	quest.71484AC8A112CDDE.title: "Devour the King"
	quest.71CE5C053B3E2572.quest_desc: [
		"You woke it; now it wants you (our interpretation: in the anime it is Milim who ends it, episode 19). A calamity does not distinguish between those who wake it and those it was sent for. Fight it anyway, and make sure that when the water settles you are the one still standing."
	]
	quest.71CE5C053B3E2572.quest_subtitle: "Defeat Charybdis"
	quest.71CE5C053B3E2572.title: "Survive the Whirlpool"
	quest.726B82305E098613.quest_desc: [
		"The ogres have become kijin, the lizardmen have begged Tempest for help, and the Orc Lord's name is on every lip (anime season 1, episodes 10-12). Benimaru has laid out the marsh on the council table: two hundred thousand orcs under a king whose skill, Starved, drives the whole horde mad with hunger."
		""
		"You have blunted the first wave and carried Act II to Tempest. Walk into the council longhouse and hear the plan before you choose your road."
	]
	quest.726B82305E098613.quest_subtitle: "Act III begins"
	quest.726B82305E098613.title: "The War Council"
	quest.7289055E6D3B5177.quest_desc: [
		"Dwarf smiths prize magic ore, iron soaked in magicules over centuries, and mine it deep under the Canaat Mountains. Mine a magic ore yourself and carry eight shards."
	]
	quest.7289055E6D3B5177.title: "Ore, But Magic?!"
	quest.72ED01B72020F604.quest_desc: [
		"The lizardmen live on the shores of Lake Siss in a village on stilts, and fish the lake. Their chief's son Gabiru came to Tempest with an envoy: the orc horde is coming and the marsh cannot hold. Travel east to the stilt village."
	]
	quest.72ED01B72020F604.quest_subtitle: "Gabiru's envoy"
	quest.72ED01B72020F604.title: "The Stilt Village"
	quest.7307AB7291AA44FF.quest_desc: [
		"Light the portal and enter the Mortal End. Its dragon waits; there is no way back up but victory or death."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor: reaching the Mortal End adds 30 Valor karma, once."
	]
	quest.7307AB7291AA44FF.title: "The Mortal End"
	quest.778998349EB8E5BE.quest_desc: [
		"Find an elytra in an end ship above an end city: the one thing in the End that is a gift, not a threat."
		""
		"&7&o“They say the wings were left behind by whoever built the city. They say it with a look at the sky.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly: but flight does not count as exploration, so the squares you walked still count."
	]
	quest.778998349EB8E5BE.title: "A Gift of Wings"
	quest.7797476042AAC217.quest_desc: [
		"Reach 10,000 EP (A-Class). The orc horde is made of thousands of fighters of B-Class and below; to cross that army you need to stand above it."
	]
	quest.7797476042AAC217.title: "A Hazard to Others"
	quest.77B55FED87C57904.quest_desc: [
		"Treyni is the dryad who keeps the forest, the one who first asked Rimuru to end the Orc Lord (anime season 1, episode 11). Her shrine is on the far eastern edge of the forest, well beyond the orc camp. She knows the calamity's name and she will say it once."
		""
		"The way is long (the shrine is about two thousand blocks east of Tempest). Go to the grove and stand in her shrine."
	]
	quest.77B55FED87C57904.quest_subtitle: "A long road east (optional)"
	quest.77B55FED87C57904.title: "Treyni's Warning"
	quest.78E241CB36B19CE3.quest_desc: [
		"Smelt iron and make an iron pickaxe. Now diamonds, and the Nether, are within reach."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Craft: mining diamonds and ancient debris, smithing and anvil work all add Craft karma."
	]
	quest.78E241CB36B19CE3.title: "Iron Age"
	quest.7933597AF82AA147.quest_desc: [
		"Brew a potion."
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Faith: every use of a brewing stand adds a little Faith karma."
	]
	quest.7933597AF82AA147.title: "Local Brewery"
	quest.7979AD4574139B8D.quest_desc: [
		"Saddle a strider, ride it with a warped fungus on a stick across a lava sea. Do not drop the stick."
		""
		"&7&o“A strider does not know it is crossing lava. This is why it is so calm.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Faith for the advancement (+2)."
	]
	quest.7979AD4574139B8D.title: "A Ride on the Lava"
	quest.7A6426F393DE80CB.quest_desc: [
		"The Society takes in anyone and asks one thing in return: that it stays hidden. A toll keeps the hidden road open and the watchers elsewhere. Pay it in bronze, the one coin every nation accepts without asking where it came from."
		""
		"Hand in six bronze coins at the fork."
	]
	quest.7A6426F393DE80CB.quest_subtitle: "Silence is paid for"
	quest.7A6426F393DE80CB.title: "The Society's Toll"
	quest.7A865EDF634D7260.quest_desc: [
		"Own two white beds. Other players and the odd traveller will come through; a house that has a spare bed is a friend's house."
		""
		"&7&o“In the Realm you do not ask a stranger's name before you give them a bed. You ask it at breakfast.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly: but a bed slept in is a night survived (Longevity), and a guest warmed is a good deed the book cannot see."
	]
	quest.7A865EDF634D7260.title: "A Bed for Every Guest"
	quest.7AF1B198048D79AD.quest_desc: [
		"Cross the basalt deltas and gather sixteen basalt. Spouts of lava, magma cubes and cliffs; walk slowly."
		""
		"&7&o“The deltas are the one place in the Nether where the scenery looks as if it was designed to kill you.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Valor for the walking."
	]
	quest.7AF1B198048D79AD.title: "The Basalt Deltas"
	quest.7B07802E34A14C2D.quest_desc: [
		"Dwargon's merchants buy monster leather, ore and crafted goods, and pay in coin. Sell something to a dwarf trader and walk away with coins in your pocket."
	]
	quest.7B07802E34A14C2D.title: "Dwarven Trade Goods"
	quest.7B8AF58B7957A204.quest_desc: [
		"Yellow banners with a red emblem hang from the arch where the outer road begins, and a watch tower stands beside it. Dwargon watches who comes to its gate. Walk through the arch."
	]
	quest.7B8AF58B7957A204.title: "The Checkpoint Arch"
	quest.7BB9FFA852D08BF6.quest_desc: [
		"Five hundred goblins eat a lot, and Shion's cooking is not a plan. The raised store on stilts in the north-east of the town keeps rats and beasts out. Hand in 32 wheat and 16 cooked porkchops to start the winter stock."
	]
	quest.7BB9FFA852D08BF6.title: "Fill the Food Store"
	quest.7C0600E97AB2B3FD.quest_desc: [
		"The forest is full of monsters with magicules of their own. Hunt a horned rabbit and a giant ant."
	]
	quest.7C0600E97AB2B3FD.title: "Monsters of Jura"
	quest.7C37E329D60483D7.quest_desc: [
		"The goblins' campfire is where the old quarter eats and decides things. To sit there you bring something for the pot; nobody asks what you have done, only whether you came with hands full."
		""
		"Stand at the campfire and hand in eight cooked beef."
	]
	quest.7C37E329D60483D7.quest_subtitle: "Rigurd's table"
	quest.7C37E329D60483D7.title: "A Seat at the Fire"
	quest.7C5E6C3E343092F0.quest_desc: [
		"Travellers queue in fenced lanes between two guard booths while the dwarf guards check what they carry. Rimuru's first visit ended in a scuffle by this gate and a night in a cell. Behave better: wait in the queue in front of the white wall."
	]
	quest.7C5E6C3E343092F0.title: "The Gate Inspection"
	quest.7C636164D8F4EF8B.quest_desc: [
		"Souei scouted the horde before anyone drew a blade: tens of thousands, all of them starving. Creep to the camp south-east of the lake and see for yourself before you pick a fight."
	]
	quest.7C636164D8F4EF8B.title: "Scouting the Orc Camp"
	quest.7C7AC7C8446F66E0.quest_desc: [
		"Harvest four pumpkins and eight sugar cane from the water's edge. Sugar and gourds are the start of every feast."
		""
		"&7&o“In autumn the road to the next village is lined with orange lanterns that are not lanterns at all.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Not scored directly."
	]
	quest.7C7AC7C8446F66E0.title: "Sweet and Gourd"
	quest.7C8D91299A01DF8D.quest_desc: [
		"A house without a door is only a frame. Hand in six oak doors so the first families can sleep behind walls instead of canvas."
	]
	quest.7C8D91299A01DF8D.title: "Doors for the New Houses"
	quest.7D36EB729E2C654D.quest_desc: [
		"Breed any two animals: feed a pair their favourite food and wait for the heart cloud."
		""
		"&7&o“The herders' rule is the oldest in the Realm: you never keep only one of a kind.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Order (0.5 per animal bred) and Faith for the advancement (+2)."
	]
	quest.7D36EB729E2C654D.title: "Two by Two"
	quest.7D48E319627565BE.quest_desc: [
		"Rigurd led the goblins through the direwolf years and still lives in the old chief's hut, north-east of the green. In the story he is the one who says what Tempest needs and keeps his word to the end. A goblin's trust is a seat at his fire."
		""
		"Stand at his door: the Oath is only words until someone sees you keep it."
	]
	quest.7D48E319627565BE.quest_subtitle: "The light road"
	quest.7D48E319627565BE.title: "Rigurd's Trust"
	quest.7D4B44AC33270DB2.quest_desc: [
		"A king does not bow to the road you walk; if you want his seat you have to take it. Gazel said as much himself."
		""
		"Claim the reward at the throne to wake the King, or strike the seated statue (the fight begins either way)."
		""
		"&6If the call fails&r (the King is already out, or resting: 72 hours), type /ttl story fight gazel_dwargo at the throne."
	]
	quest.7D4B44AC33270DB2.quest_subtitle: "The loud way"
	quest.7D4B44AC33270DB2.title: "Take the Throne"
	quest.7DB517E89CB02955.quest_desc: [
		"Small coins buy bread; a gold coin buys a sword. Earn your first gold coin in trade with the dwarves."
	]
	quest.7DB517E89CB02955.title: "My Precious"
	quest.7F12E567F376A418.quest_desc: [
		"Slay a hostile creature, and put an arrow into something. The Voice of the World notices a soul that learns to fight."
		""
		"&7&o“A mortal who has never been afraid has never been in the Realm after dark.”&r"
		""
		"&6Next life:&r Faith for each advancement (+2 each); Valor for every new kind of foe slain (+4 each)."
	]
	quest.7F12E567F376A418.title: "First Blood"
